PVD("thailand_ndp_2012-2016",{"docs":["","TH 11th Plan 2011 16 THAI"],"s":{"1":[[1,"2","4","Eleventh National Economic and Social Development Plan Implementation","the Cabinet ... has decided that this Plan should be implemented as the national guidelines for economic and social development policies.",""],[1,"3","2","Stakeholder Participation in Plan Implementation","the Eleventh Plan will be implemented using the insights and involvement of all stakeholders.",""],[1,"8","4","Thai Khem-Kaeng Investment Allocation Scheme","Investment initiatives under the \"Thai Khem-Kaeng\" (Strong Thailand) scheme in 2012 was a program designed to allocate investments appropriately by considering economic, social and environmental dimensions, and it covered every sector.",""],[1,"32","3","Monetary and Financial Management Strengthening","Priority should be given to financial management following a monetary policy that is appropriate and timely.",""],[1,"32","3","Capital Market Development Promotion","The role of the capital market should be promoted to be consistent with development in the global financial sector.",""],[1,"32","3","Economic Surveillance and Early Warning System","A surveillance mechanism for economic fluctuations and a comprehensive warning system should be established.",""],[1,"32","3","Public Revenue Collection System Improvement","There is a need to improve efficiency in foreign capital management as well as fiscal management through an improved public revenue collection system.",""],[1,"32","3","Budget Allocation and Management Reform","More effective budget allocation and management is also crucial to prevent fiscal risks and enhance the operational efficiency of state-owned enterprises.",""],[1,"32","3","Private Sector Participation in Infrastructure and Public Services","The private sector should display increased participation in infrastructure investment and providing public services.",""],[1,"32","3","Local Government Fiscal Capacity Enhancement","The fiscal capacity of local government should also be increased.",""]],"2":[[1,"37","3","Plan Translation Handbook Development","a handbook for plan translation should be designed for implementation.",""],[1,"38","1","Information Technology for Public Participation and Database Management","information technology should be used to assist communication and develop database management in order to encourage public participation in the development process.",""],[1,"38","4","National Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","Developing efficient, transparent and participatory systems of monitoring and evaluation at all levels.",""],[1,"170","3","Inclusive Multi-Stakeholder Planning and Coordination Committees","many stakeholders could participate as committee members in, for example, the National Rural Development Committee, the Eastern Seaboard Committee, and the Joint Public-Private Committee.",""],[1,"170","3","Policy Formulation, Implementation, and Monitoring Committees","Such groups were responsible for outlining policies and formulating and implementing plans.",""],[1,"170","3","Stakeholder-Coordinated Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","They were also charged to monitor and evaluate by coordinating with appropriate stakeholders as development partners.",""],[1,"170","3","Agency-Led Budget Proposal and Action Planning","Budget proposals were initiated by each agency in accordance with its work plan, and agencies established action plans that were more responsive to the national one.",""],[1,"171","4","Local Planning Integration Support Mechanism","Now there needs to be a local connecting point so integration can proceed to the planning and implementation stages.",""],[1,"175","3","Community Coordination for Data Collection and Development Planning","Community coordination should be encouraged to collect data, to undertake mutual analyses to support decision-making and to draft community development plans.",""],[1,"175","3","Multi-Stakeholder Development Network Formation","they can create development networks with the public and private sectors, scholars and LAOs to solve social problems and address disparities.",""],[1,"175","5","Step-by-Step Plan Implementation with Public Participation","The fundamental principle to translate the Eleventh Plan into action is to proceed step-by-step while creating universal understanding and nationwide public participation.",""],[1,"175","5","Integration of the Plan with Government Policies","This will facilitate integration of the Plan with government policies and other actions.",""],[1,"175","5","Community Participation in Development Process","The Thai people, communities and organizations throughout society will be encouraged to take part in the development process by using knowledge that relates to their socio-geographic conditions.",""],[1,"175","5","Fair and Just Plan Implementation","Implementation will be done fairly and justly.",""],[1,"176","1","Eleventh Plan Implementation at All Levels","Impel national achievement by pursuing the Eleventh Plan as the main thrust for translating the plan into action at all levels, as they relate to socio-geographic conditions.",""],[1,"176","2","Area-Based Development Distribution Approach","Distribute the benefits of progress to the area level by using the AFP approach.",""],[1,"176","4","Stakeholder Network and Cluster Development","Networks and clusters should be created to respond to local needs.",""],[1,"176","5","Popular Participation in Eleventh Plan Implementation","To implement the Eleventh Plan through popular participation.",""],[1,"176","7","Progress Monitoring and Evaluation System","To monitor and systematically evaluate progress at all levels - national, regional and local.",""],[1,"176","9","Plan-Do-Check-Act Plan Management System","The efficient management of the Eleventh Plan will apply the concept of Plan-Do-Check-Act (P-D- C-A).",""],[1,"177","13","Plan Implementation Mechanisms and Tools Development","Develop mechanisms, methods and tools for effectively translating the plan into action and create facilities for the implementation",""],[1,"177","19","Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","Developing M&E system and indicators for effectively inspecting the implementation",""],[1,"177","21","Development Partner Engagement and Plan Communication","The Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB) will create mutual understanding of the Plan's goals with all development partners through these processes and methods:","Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB)"],[1,"177","22","Plan Communication and Public Relations Campaign","Establish a line of communication to create awareness of the Plan and acceptance that it is an effective tool for integrated development that can be applied by all development partners.",""],[1,"177","23","Political Party and Government Policy Integration Initiative","Politicians will be encouraged to integrate major advancement issues into the policies of their political parties and the government.",""],[1,"177","24","Citizen Implementation Handbook","Prepare an implementation handbook for citizens in order to stimulate participation.",""],[1,"179","1","Plan Alignment and Synchronized Implementation Mechanism","Link the Eleventh Plan's concepts, strategies, development issues and specific proposals with government policies, the Government Administrative Plan and other plans.",""],[1,"182","3","Development Database Creation and Maintenance","Economic, social, natural resource and environmental databases will be developed and kept up to date.",""],[1,"182","5","Development Partner Coordination for Plan Implementation","The NESDB is charged with creating understanding and coordinating development partners with the plan implementation committees at all levels so that they can apply the Plan properly as follows:",""],[1,"182","6","National Committee Coordination for Eleventh Plan Implementation","Development agencies will coordinate their work through national committees responsible for high-priority missions that involve many dimensions of progress, for example, (a) the National Creative Economy Policy Committee, (b) the Joint Public-Private Consultative Committee on Economic Problems, (c) the National Water Resources Committee, and (d) the Thailand National Logistics Committee.",""],[1,"183","2","Province-Led Plan Translation and Evaluation Mechanism","Use the province as a focal point to translate the Eleventh Plan into action, and evaluate it.",""],[1,"183","3","Public-Private and Stakeholder Coordination for Implementation","Coordinate collaboration between the private sector and government agencies in the implementation process.",""],[1,"185","3","Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","Develop an efficient, transparent and participatory system of monitoring and evaluation at all levels.",""],[1,"185","4","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation System","Encourage continuous monitoring and evaluation that focuses on the objectives and targets of the Plan.",""],[1,"185","5","Eleventh Plan Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","Develop monitoring and evaluation systems for the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"185","6","Overall Monitoring and Evaluation System for Implementation","Develop an overall monitoring and evaluation system for implementation.",""],[1,"185","7","Local Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop means to monitor and evaluate at the local level.",""],[1,"185","7","Area-Based Evaluation and Inspection System","The Policy Committee for Integrative Provincial and Clustering of Province Administration (PCC) and the Regional Supervision Committee should create evaluation systems for area-based achievement and improve the main inspection system so it will be an efficient tool to qualify and quantify implementation.",""],[1,"185","7","Inspector-General Monitoring Apparatus","A main apparatus composed of the inspectors-general of the ministries will be established to monitor the process of Plan formulation, the participation of all parties, and budget utilization.",""],[1,"185","8","Citizen Inspection and Monitoring Mechanism","Strengthen an inspection mechanism for citizens to use to monitor and evaluate.",""],[1,"186","1","Community Project Monitoring and Audit Participation","take part in auditing the progress, transparency and achievement of development projects in their communities.",""],[1,"186","1","Information Technology and Data Management Capacity Development","Each individual's potential should be developed in information technology and data management in order to monitor projects.",""],[1,"186","2","Monitoring and Evaluation Database Development","Develop an efficient database to help monitor and evaluate.",""],[1,"186","3","Government Information Networks and Comprehensive Database Development","Create a comprehensive database.",""],[1,"186","4","Local-Level Database Development and Technical Assistance","Establish databases at the local level, that is, information systems that identify individual potential, community organizations, and civil society.",""],[1,"186","5","Central-Local Information Network Linkage System","Link information networks between central and local levels.",""]],"3":[[1,"24","2","Public Sector Improvement and Good Governance Reform","Meanwhile, fairness within the national administration is promoted through good governance with emphasis on the improvement of the public sector and the quality of government officials.",""],[1,"24","2","Decentralization Strengthening for Local Administration","Decentralization should be pursued more effectively in order to strengthen local administration.",""],[1,"28","2","Public Administration Reform and Civil Service Capacity Development","Efficient public administration must be enhanced through a thorough system of checks and balances while professionally capable, ethical, and responsible officials should be developed for government service.",""]],"4":[[1,"24","2","Fair Access to Justice and Public Resources","People should have fair access to the judicial system and public resources while democratic values and good governance are to be promoted.",""],[1,"28","2","Judicial Access and Remedy Improvement","The judicial system should guarantee impartiality, provide more access for complaints to be submitted and allow for remedies for affected victims.",""]],"5":[[1,"14","3","Macroeconomic Management Law and Regulation Reform","there will be an initiative to reform laws and regulations governing macroeconomic management so as to encourage a foundation for the economy and its growth that has strength and quality.",""],[1,"178","3","Good Governance and Just Society Initiative","9) to enhance good governance to promote a just society.",""],[1,"181","5","Regulatory Amendments for Efficient Plan Execution","Amend regulations to enable efficient execution of the Plan at every level.",""],[1,"181","5","Public Finance Act Amendment","the draft Public Finance Act B.E ..... to support efficiency and transparency in monetary policy",""],[1,"182","2","Information Technology for Development Partner Coordination","Apply information technology as a tool to assist communication and create links among development partners.",""],[1,"182","4","Public Participation Channels for Development Planning","Introduce channels for public participation in the development process that cover both policy and performance.",""],[1,"182","4","Civil Society Forum and Dialogue Support","Public spaces will be available so development partners can organize forums such as the Civil Society Forum and Dialogue.",""],[1,"182","4","Online Development Information and Participation Network","Online networks will share information and participate in development activities.",""],[1,"182","7","Public Administration Efficiency Improvement","Improve the efficiency of the methods and processes of public administration to be more efficient.",""],[1,"185","1","Reform of Government Personnel Roles and Work Methods","Amend roles of government personnel and their work methods to support overall development and encourage regional government agencies to be coordinators.",""],[1,"185","1","Strategy Manager Institution Establishment","Institutions that develop strategy managers should be established to create a \"change agent\" to share knowledge and execute plans.",""],[1,"185","2","Civil Society and International Cooperation Forums","International forums to share knowledge should be organized, especially for countries involved in regional and subregional cooperation.",""],[1,"185","2","Technical and Innovative Cooperation Promotion","Cooperation in technical and innovative fields should be encouraged to support domestic and international growth.",""]],"6":[[1,"24","2","Anti-Corruption Mechanisms with Public Participation","Anti-corruption mechanisms and preventive systems with popular participation and input should be developed.",""],[1,"78","3","Public Access to Government Procurement, Budget, and Project Information","Information sources should be developed to disclose data on government procurement, budgets, and projects.",""],[1,"78","3","Citizen Oversight of Government and Local Administration","The general public should monitor and scrutinize government and local administrative organizations.",""],[1,"78","3","Government Open Data and Right-to-Information Provision","The government sector should provide accurate data and other information, and acknowledge the citizen's right to access this information.",""],[1,"154","1","Law Enforcement Strengthening","It is essential that law enforcement effectiveness be strengthened.",""],[1,"154","1","Anti-Corruption Reform","Corruption must be eliminated.",""],[1,"154","1","Transparent and Equitable Resource Allocation","Resource allocation should be thorough, equitable and transparent.",""],[1,"154","1","Regional and Local Government Capacity Reinforcement","The capacity of government agencies at regional and local levels should be reinforced.",""]],"7":[[1,"178","4","Strategic Investment Planning Framework","Integrate development issues to formulate specific strategic investment plans.",""],[1,"178","5","Investment Planning and Budget Allocation for Growth","Formulate investment plans for growth by considering priorities in the Eleventh Plan's strategy that reflect proper budget allocation for overall achievement.",""],[1,"178","6","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Mega Projects","Encourage Public-Private Partnerships (PPP) in mega- projects such as infrastructure development and logistics systems.",""],[1,"178","7","Ministerial Plan Integration of Tasks, Targets, and Indicators","Translate development issues into action through Ministerial Plans by integrating main tasks that have concrete targets and key indicators into the Plans.","NESDB | relevant agencies"],[1,"179","19","Three-Year Development Plan Formulation","LAO formulate three year development plan (after announcing four-year provincial/cluster development plan)",""],[1,"179","23","Integration of Eleventh Plan Priorities into Government Policies and Administrative Planning","The government will integrate high priority development issues and specific items under the Eleventh Plan with their own policies and present these to the Parliament.",""],[1,"179","23","Integration of the Eleventh Plan into Budget Allocation Strategies","Central government agencies have integrated the Eleventh Plan into budget allocation strategies in order to provide the framework for ministries who request a budget to support their four-year and annual action plans.",""],[1,"180","5","Participatory Budget Allocation Strategy","Create a budget allocation strategy that utilizes participation.",""],[1,"180","6","Budget Advocacy for Eleventh Plan Priorities","The Bureau of the Budget and NESDB should advocate the significant issues of the Eleventh Plan as they relate to budget allocation.","The Bureau of the Budget | NESDB"],[1,"180","6","National Program and Project Implementation and M&E Guidelines","guidelines to realize programs and projects and to monitor and evaluate national development at all levels should be approved by the Cabinet and the Parliament.",""],[1,"181","1","Guidelines for Budget Allocation Supporting Local Development Plans","The Bureau of the Budget, NESDB and all involved agencies should work closely on guidelines for budget allocation to support local, provincial and cluster development plans.","The Bureau of the Budget | NESDB | all involved agencies"],[1,"181","1","Government-Wide Budget Planning Coordination and Understanding Process","The process of creating understanding has to be carried out by all government agencies so that the links between development plans and the budget system, from the national to local levels can be comprehended.","all government agencies"],[1,"181","1","Inclusive Budgeting Process for Development Partners","representatives of all development partners should participate in the budgeting process from management through evaluation in order to respond to local demands.",""]],"8":[[1,"37","1","Area, Function and Participation Planning Approach","In order to achieve the vision, mission and targets, the implementation of the Eleventh plan should be designed in accordance with national, regional and local agendas.",""],[1,"37","2","Cluster-Based Collaborative Development Planning","all development partners should collaborate through the cluster approach, and be responsive to problem solving and area development.",""],[1,"37","4","Integration of the Eleventh Plan into Government and Local Planning","Significant development issues in the Plan should be incorporated or integrated into government policies, the Government Administrative Plan, specific plans and operational plans.",""],[1,"38","2","Integration of Plan Priorities into Agency Agendas","National committees and agencies are encouraged to integrate the Plan's development issues and guidelines into their agendas.",""],[1,"38","2","Provincial Development Coordination and Clearing House Mechanism","Provincial organizations should serve to link, coordinate and act as clearing houses for top-down and bottom-up development issues for the private sector and for other agencies that collaborate in the implementation process.",""],[1,"59","4","Integrated Top-Down and Bottom-Up Development Planning","Adjust the development process to integrate top-down and bottom-up approaches.",""],[1,"80","3","Area-Based Development Integration and Multi-Sector Partnership Coordination","The main focus should be to integrate area-based development and the roles of development partners from all sectors, including the political and public sectors, the community, and civil society.",""],[1,"173","2","University and Research Agency Community Cooperation","it is therefore as important to encourage educational institutions and research agencies to cooperate with communities on matters relevant to each particular area",""],[1,"173","2","Local Organization Self-Directed Development Support","it is therefore as important ... to encourage local organizations to choose and propel their own growth issues",""],[1,"173","2","Regional Research for Local Development","institutions at the regional level should be encouraged to strongly incorporate research efforts directed toward local progress",""],[1,"174","4","Decentralization and Local Government Resource Allocation Reform","The public sector has new tools and techniques of decentralization.",""],[1,"174","5","Local Citizen Participation in Governance Mechanisms","Citizens at the local level have been empowered with more opportunities to participate in the national administration.",""],[1,"180","2","Integrated Provincial and Cluster Development Planning","The regional offices of many ministries have incorporated programs and projects, and a budget for them, into provincial and cluster development plans using the main ideas of the integrated provincial administration guidelines under the Royal Decree on Integrated-Provincial and Clustering Development B.E. 2551.",""],[1,"180","2","Cabinet-Approved Provincial and Cluster Development Compliance","To comply with the principle of the Decree, agencies that are involved must plan their developments in accordance with the provincial and cluster improvement plans that are approved by the Cabinet.",""],[1,"180","3","Provincial and Cluster Development Planning","Provinces and clusters will formulate development plans that comply with government policies, the Eleventh Plan and Regional Development Guidelines.",""],[1,"180","3","Provincial and Cluster Needs Assessment","In addition, they will analyze problems and needs in order to identify development issues in provincial and cluster development plans.",""],[1,"180","4","Local Needs-Responsive Development Programming","LAOs have proposed programs and projects that respond to local needs, following action at the provincial level.",""],[1,"180","4","Local Problem Survey and Development Issue Analysis","Tambon Administration Organizations (TAOs) have surveyed and analyzed local problems and needs, identified development issues, and then accomplished their tasks under local administration laws.",""],[1,"180","4","Provincial Development Coordination and Project Identification","Meanwhile, Provincial Administrative Organizations (PAOs) would coordinate preparations for local developments and identify significant projects that are beyond the capacity of LAO's to operate using Provincial Plans.",""],[1,"181","2","Private Sector Development Partnership Integration","Encourage the private sector to integrate important development issues when they formulate their business investment plans.",""],[1,"181","2","Joint Public-Private Consultative Committee Strengthening","This will create development partnerships while also promoting the Joint Public-Private Consultative Committee on Economic Problems (JPPCC) as a key mechanism to link the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"181","2","Delegation to Provincial and Cluster Joint Committees","The JPPCC will have to delegate more responsibilities to provincial and cluster joint committees, and consider national strategies as they link to local needs.",""],[1,"181","5","Decentralization to Local Government Organization Plan","the formulation of the Decentralization to Local Government Organization Plan (Third Edition)",""],[1,"181","5","Decentralization Action Plan for Local Administrative Organizations","the Determining Process of Decentralization to Local Administrative Organizations Action Plan (Third Edition) under",""],[1,"184","2","Local Administrative Organization Capacity Strengthening","In order to perform their duties efficiently, the capability of LAOs should be enhanced and their administration simplified and made more flexible.",""],[1,"184","3","Regional University Community Development Engagement","Encourage regional universities and vocational institutions to participate in community development.",""],[1,"184","3","University Research Application for Community Progress","Universities should apply research output and serve to coordinate community progress.",""],[1,"184","3","Cluster-Based Local Development Approach","The cluster concept should be employed.",""],[1,"184","3","Vocational Skills Training for Local Development","Vocational institutions should provide training in technological skills to assist local development.",""],[1,"184","4","Private Sector Corporate Governance and Social Partnership Promotion","Corporate governance should be emphasized, business targets should be linked to the nation's development, and proactive cooperation and creativity should be promoted along with corporate social responsibility.",""],[1,"184","4","Private Sector Community and Knowledge Institution Alliances","The private sector should form alliances with communities, non-governmental organizations (NGOs) and academic institutions to bring about collaboration in social activities.",""],[1,"184","5","Constructive Media Messaging Promotion","Encourage the media to deliver constructive messages.",""],[1,"184","6","NGO Participation in Development Activities","The public sector will encourage them to participate greatly in development activities.",""],[1,"185","1","Provincial Development Partnership Coordination","Provincial organizations should join with development partners to work toward common goals, respond to national strategies, solve problems and develop potential at the local and community levels.",""]],"9":[[1,"80","1","Public Sector Personnel Development and Integrity Incentives","Develop public sector personnel that are qualified, ethical, and highly responsible.",""],[1,"91","5","Systematic Public Sector Human Resource Planning and Development","Promote systematic human resource planning and development, and define the precise roles and job descriptions of officials, employees, and temporary officials in the public sector to increase efficiency and improve human resource administration to achieve greater morality, integrity, and good governance.",""]],"10":[[1,"120","4","Intellectual Property Awareness and Commercialization Promotion","Encourage registration, protection and commercialization of intellectual property to drive creative business growth by making the public aware of the importance of intellectual property and of concerns related to creating value added, enhancing business growth, and upgrading standards of goods and services in every sector.",""],[1,"120","4","Intellectual Property Administrative Simplification and Enforcement","Moreover, reduce red tape in the bureaucratic process of the acquisition of intellectual property rights and strictly enforce laws related to intellectual property.",""],[1,"122","5","Intellectual Property Registration and Protection Mechanism","An intellectual property protocol should be encouraged through establishment of a mechanism to facilitate patent and copyright registration abroad, while building an efficient intellectual property system that protects rights in those patents registered abroad.",""],[1,"124","6","Intellectual Property Management System Development","Develop an intellectual property management system.",""],[1,"124","6","Intellectual Property Registration and Protection Promotion","Promote registration, utilization and protection of intellectual property rights in order to encourage research, innovation, creativity and local insight that benefit commercial applications to help drive the economy.",""],[1,"124","7","Intellectual Property Awareness Campaign","Create awareness in all sectors, particularly in businesses, of the importance of intellectual property such as patents, trademarks and",""],[1,"125","2","Intellectual Property Legal and Enforcement Reform","Improve legal measures, protection mechanisms and law enforcement governing intellectual property to eliminate intellectual property violations and support fair sharing of profits.",""],[1,"125","3","Intellectual Property Registration Streamlining","Streamline and accelerate the process of registration in order to facilitate owners of research work, innovations, local wisdom and creativity to acquire intellectual property rights and be able to respond to market demand in a timely manner.",""]],"11":[[1,"28","2","Social Media Support for Local and National Development","the use of social media should be supported to reinforce development at both local and national levels.",""]],"12":[[1,"14","3","Economic Restructuring for Quality and Sustainable Growth","Measures will be designed to generate favorable conditions and fair competition; restructure trade and investment to meet the needs of domestic and international markets; add value for potential products in the service sector; transform the industrial sector into knowledge-based and eco-friendly industries; and improve infrastructure and logistic systems.",""],[1,"23","3","Knowledge, Science, Technology, Innovation and Creativity Development","In all aspects, the powerhouse of the country's future development will comprise knowledge, science, technology, innovation and creativity.",""],[1,"24","1","Domestic Economic Strengthening through Science, Technology and Creativity","Second, strengthening of economic capital, in both physical and financial aspects, is concerned with establishing a strong domestic economy through the application of wisdom, science, technology and creativity.",""],[1,"25","10","Technology- and Innovation-Led Economic Upgrading","To develop an efficient and sustainable economy by upgrading production and services based on technology, innovation and creativity using effective regional links, by improving food and energy security, and by upgrading eco-friendly production and consumption toward a low-carbon society.",""],[1,"31","4","Science, Technology, Innovation and Creativity for Economic Restructuring","Utilize science, technology, innovation and creativity as fundamental elements in economic restructuring.",""],[1,"31","4","Service Sector Restructuring for Higher Value Creation","The service sector should be restructured to allow for higher value creation and to become more environmentally healthy based on innovation and creativity.",""],[1,"31","4","Creative Economy Promotion for Creative Businesses, Cities and Industries","An economy based on creativity should be promoted with its focus on creative businesses, cities and industries.",""],[1,"31","4","Knowledge-Based and Environmentally Sound Industrial Development","There is also a need to use science, technology and creativity to promote quality and sustainability in the industrial sector and to move Thailand's development increasingly toward industries that are knowledge-based and environmentally sound.",""],[1,"32","1","Research, Technology Transfer, and Innovation Commercialization Support","emphasized in research and development, technology transfers and applications that lead to commercialization of innovation and improve the quality of life.",""],[1,"32","1","Creative Thinking and Local Knowledge Development","Also, focus on the development of creative thinking and application of local knowledge.",""],[1,"32","1","Public-Private Enabling Infrastructure for Value Creation","The public and private sectors should cooperate to create an improved environment that enables value creation by providing appropriate infrastructure and facilities, thus encouraging technological development and innovation.",""],[1,"56","1","Trade and Investment Policy Revision","Trade and investment policies should be revised to serve economic expansion in Asia, the Middle East, Africa and the domestic economy.",""],[1,"56","1","Industrial Innovation and Clean Production Upgrade","Industry should be redirected to focus on technology, innovation, creativity and environmentally sound production.",""],[1,"56","3","Economic Restructuring Mechanisms","Develop mechanisms for economic restructuring in order to increase competitiveness and fair competition.",""],[1,"56","5","ASEAN Economic Community Preparedness and Competitiveness Enhancement","5.6 Prepare Thailand for the ASEAN Economic Community (AEC).",""],[1,"57","1","ASEAN Compliance Regulatory and Institutional Reform","Regulations and institutional management should be made to comply with ASEAN's rules.",""],[1,"64","3","Trade and Investment Sector Restructuring","Thailand needs to restructure the trade and investment sectors that are relevant to domestic and foreign markets.",""],[1,"64","3","Manufacturing Sector Innovation Transformation","Science, technology and innovation should be employed to transform production in the manufacturing sector so that it is knowledge-based, creativity-oriented and environmentally healthy.",""],[1,"64","3","Legal and Regulatory Reform","Reform of laws and regulatory rules is necessary.",""],[1,"64","3","Efficient Macroeconomic Management","The macroeconomy should be managed efficiently.",""],[1,"76","1","SME Technology Upgrading for Competitiveness","Technology should be upgraded to increase competitiveness of SMEs in the new global marketplace.",""],[1,"115","3","Economic Structure Reform for Inclusive Growth","Reform the economic structure to achieve inclusive growth.",""],[1,"115","7","Economic Activity Expansion and Inflation Stabilization Policy","Expand the suitable and stable economic activities, and maintain an average annual inflation rate that does not exceed 3.5 percent.",""],[1,"115","9","Agriculture, Agro-industry, Services, and Responsible Manufacturing Upgrade","Increase the proportion of agriculture and agro-industry sectors in the GDP so they do not go lower than 16 percent, the proportion of the service sectors no lower than 50 percent, and upgrade the manufacturing industry to be more community and environmentally responsible while maintaining high value.",""],[1,"116","1","Research and Development Funding Increase","Increase funding of research and development to at least 1 percent of GDP and up to 2 percent in the future.",""],[1,"121","1","Manufacturing Structural Reform for Inclusive Growth","Develop manufacturing by implementing structural reforms with inclusive growth.",""]],"13":[[1,"118","3","SME Human Resource Skills Support Programme","Emphasis should be on the development of SMEs by providing support for building human resource skills that are relevant to business requirements.",""],[1,"118","3","SME Productivity and Innovation Capacity Development","Improve the knowledge and skills of firms in production, marketing and IT, and promote the application of science and technology, local insight, innovation and good governance.",""],[1,"118","3","SME Finance Access Support Measures","Further, measures should be established to assist SMEs in gaining access to sources of finance.",""],[1,"118","6","Skills Upgrading and International Standards Compliance","The skills and talents of personnel should be expanded, and businesses and professionals should meet international standards.",""],[1,"123","6","Inclusive Financial Access and SME Support Measures","Encourage equal access to financial resources at reasonable cost.",""],[1,"123","7","Grassroots Financial Services Capacity and Linkage Mechanism","The operational capabilities of community financial organizations and cooperatives at all levels should be developed to meet standards of responsibility.",""],[1,"123","7","Microfinance Fund Linkage Mechanism","Mechanisms should be put in place to link funds among microfinance groups, and between microfinance groups and financial institutions in order to foster money saving habits and sound financial management at the household level.",""],[1,"124","1","Financial Literacy and Household Savings Promotion","Provide knowledge and information about finance by imposing economic discipline on the business and household sectors as well as SMEs.",""],[1,"127","5","SME and Local Enterprise Loan Access Support","SMEs and local enterprises should have access to loans.",""]],"14":[[1,"36","1","Planning for Trade and Climate Agreement Impacts","Planning should be introduced to deal with the anticipated effects from trade measures and international agreements on environment and climate change.",""],[1,"36","1","Research and Strategic Mitigation for Affected Products and Businesses","It is essential to conduct research on the effects of these threats and develop strategic plans together with alleviating measures for relevant products and businesses.",""],[1,"36","1","Export Carbon Footprint Assessment and Green Industry Incentives","Firms should consider the carbon footprint for export goods, together with provisions for incentives for new industries that will create an environment for sustainable development.",""]],"15":[[1,"118","4","Service Sector Restructuring and Value-Added Promotion","Restructure the service sector.",""],[1,"118","7","Service Sector Investment Promotion Measures","Develop enabling factors to induce investment in the service sector from both internal and external sources.",""],[1,"118","7","Service Efficiency Improvement Initiative","The efficiency of services should be improved.",""],[1,"118","7","High-Potential Business Database Development","Create databases that focus on high potential businesses.",""],[1,"118","7","Legal and Incentive Reform for Service Investment","Laws and regulations should be revised and incentives to facilitate investment should be",""],[1,"119","1","Research and Development and Knowledge Transfer Support","Research and development as well as knowledge transfer should be supported.",""],[1,"119","1","Business Information Technology Adoption Promotion","The application of information technology by businesses should be encouraged.",""],[1,"119","1","Environmentally Responsible Service Business Operations","Environmentally responsible operations should be promoted in service businesses and human resource development should reflect current needs.",""],[1,"119","1","Human Resource Development Aligned with Current Needs","Environmentally responsible operations should be promoted in service businesses and human resource development should reflect current needs.",""]],"16":[[1,"23","3","Infrastructure and Logistics System Development","In this context, infrastructure and logistic systems have to be further developed in tandem with the quality of human resources.",""],[1,"32","2","High-Quality Infrastructure and Logistics Development","In addition, the development of high quality infrastructure and logistic systems should enhance the efficiency of domestic and international connectivity that is consistent with international standards.",""],[1,"33","2","Transport and Logistics Connectivity Development","Develop connectivity in transport and logistic systems under regional cooperation frameworks.",""],[1,"33","2","Transport and Logistics Service Upgrading","This should be achieved through the development of efficient transport and logistic services that meet international standards.",""],[1,"33","2","Transport and Goods Movement Regulatory Reform","Improvement of rules and regulations governing the transportation of goods and people should also be accomplished.",""],[1,"33","2","Transport and Logistics Human Resource Capacity Building","the capabilities of human resources in transport and logistic businesses should be enhanced.",""],[1,"33","2","Border Area and Economic Zone Connectivity Enhancement","Economic connectivity along border areas and economic zones should be increased, ensuring connectivity with domestic production bases.",""],[1,"35","3","Transport and Logistics Energy Efficiency Improvement","To this end, energy efficiency in the transportation and logistic sectors should be enhanced in order to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.",""],[1,"56","4","Transportation and Logistics Network Development","Efficient transportation and logistics networks should be promoted to support trade and investment.",""],[1,"56","4","New Economic Links to South Asia","New economic links to South Asia should be created, and transit and cross border trade facilities and Border Trade Zones should be established.",""],[1,"56","4","Transit and Cross-Border Trade Facilities and Border Trade Zones","New economic links to South Asia should be created, and transit and cross border trade facilities and Border Trade Zones should be established.",""],[1,"60","2","Land Transport Infrastructure and Logistics Development","Infrastructure and logistics will be developed to improve connections by land.",""],[1,"64","3","Infrastructure and Logistics Development","Infrastructure and logistical systems should be developed further and secure energy sources established.",""],[1,"65","1","Subregional Production and Investment Connectivity Development","to the development of production and investment bases that have links to neighboring countries and to the Southeast Asia Region and include connectivity with domestic production bases.",""],[1,"65","1","Transport and Logistics System Development and Regulatory Reform","Transport and logistics systems should be developed through subregional cooperation and supported by reforming laws and regulations regarding transportation of passengers and goods.",""],[1,"105","4","Agricultural Logistics Management Improvement","Promote management of logistics to improve productivity in the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"125","5","Multimodal Transportation Development","Encourage development of multimodal transportation by advancing energy efficient forms of transportation.",""],[1,"125","5","Integrated Freight Distribution System Development","Effective distribution systems for goods should be built to reduce the overall cost of logistics.",""],[1,"125","6","Logistics Human Resource Development and Network Building","Increase the efficiency of logistics management by developing professional human resources.",""],[1,"125","6","Logistics Research and Development Regulatory Reform","Laws and regulations should be amended to foster innovative research and development in the logistics field.",""],[1,"125","6","National Single Window and Trade Facilitation Upgrade","To make trade more efficient and facilitate it, upgrade the National Single Window system, distribution centers, and cross-border trade.",""],[1,"125","6","Transport Management System Improvement","The efficiency of transport management systems should be improved.",""],[1,"125","6","Strategic Airport and Seaport Role Definition","The strategic role played by major airports and seaports should be defined in order to reduce transportation costs and increase the nation's competitiveness in the long run.",""],[1,"141","2","Regional Transport and Logistics Connectivity Development","Developing connectivity in transport and logistics systems under regional cooperation frameworks.",""],[1,"141","3","Efficient Transport and Logistics Services Development","Develop efficient transport and logistics services that meet international standards, especially roads, railways, including double track and high-speed trains, and maritime transport.",""],[1,"141","3","Customs Checkpoint and Border Crossing Facilitation Improvement","Customs checkpoints, border economic centers, and border crossing facilitation should be improved",""],[1,"141","3","Strategic Corridor Infrastructure Investment","The government will invest in strategic projects in each economic corridor, including through public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"141","4","Cross-Border Transport Rules and Regulatory Simplification","Improve rules and regulations related to the movement of goods and people by reducing the volume of documents, operation costs, and period of time needed for cross-border transport.",""],[1,"141","5","Transport and Logistics Human Resource Capacity Building","Enhance human resource capabilities in transport and logistics businesses to improve the potential of the private sector by emphasizing foreign language training and logistics management.",""],[1,"141","5","SME Cross-Border Business Development Support","The capacity of SMEs should be enhanced by providing information on joint business development with neighboring countries and by utilizing infrastructure along economic corridors and export gateways in the subregion.",""],[1,"142","1","Technical Assistance for Transport and Logistics Human Resource Development","Thailand will play a role as a development partner by providing technical assistance to neighboring countries to increase human resources in the transport and logistics businesses.",""],[1,"178","3","Subregional and Regional Development Partner Cooperation","5) to encourage cooperation of development partners at subregional and regional levels;",""]],"17":[[1,"125","7","Railway System Upgrading and Safety Improvement","Improve railway transport by upgrading the present railway system and the links between road and railway networks to increase safety.",""],[1,"125","7","Dual-Track Railway Expansion","Dual-track rail lines along major routes should be added.",""],[1,"125","7","Railway Rolling Stock and Signaling Upgrade","Locomotives and rolling stock should be provided and railway-signaling systems should be upgraded to increase efficiency for transportation of passengers and goods.",""],[1,"125","7","High-Speed Railway Development","A high speed railway should be developed to link major regional cities and ASEAN countries.",""],[1,"125","7","State Railway of Thailand Management Reform","The management structure of the State Railway of Thailand should be changed to improve efficiency and promote better services and operation in the future.",""]],"18":[[1,"126","1","Public Transportation Network Modernization","Modernize the public transportation network so that it covers more areas and responds to the expansion of urban areas and land use.",""],[1,"126","1","Electric Train Network Development","An electric train network should be built for public transportation.",""],[1,"126","1","Urban Public Transport Efficiency Improvement","The efficiency of current public transportation in Bangkok and other municipal areas should be increased.",""],[1,"126","1","Commuting Facilities Development","Facilities to support commuting patterns should be developed that serve both private cars and public transportation.",""],[1,"126","1","Regional Public Transport Service Improvement","Regional public transportation services should be improved.",""],[1,"126","1","Public Transport Governance Reform","The management structure of the overall public transportation system should be changed to improve the quality, standards, and equity of services.",""]],"19":[[1,"119","2","Tourist Attraction Rehabilitation and Quality Improvement","Rehabilitate and increase the quality of tourist attractions to improve market demand.",""],[1,"119","2","Tourism Cluster Development in High-Potential Areas","Tourism clusters in high potential areas should be created.",""],[1,"119","2","Tourism Product Diversification and Market Expansion","Activities for tourists should be promoted that fit the potential of each area.",""],[1,"119","2","Tourism Marketing Strategy Renewal","Fresh marketing strategies should attract new customers in new markets.",""],[1,"159","3","Expansion of Low-Impact Service Industries","Businesses with high potential and services with low environmental impact should be expanded; these include health care and tourism, including ecotourism.",""],[1,"159","3","Sustainable Tourism Support Measures","Development of these services should be designed so they do not harm farmers and communities, for example, support various measures for qualitative tourism in the national park and best practice in communities.",""],[1,"159","3","Local Knowledge-Based Creative Product Development","Use of local knowledge should be supported to generate creative products and services for transition to a low carbon society.",""]],"20":[[1,"119","3","Sustainable Tourism Management and Infrastructure Upgrading","Manage tourism to achieve balanced and sustainable growth by focusing on activities that are creative and environmentally friendly.",""]],"21":[[1,"145","3","Infectious Disease Prevention and Control Capacity Building","Collaborate to prevent infection and the spread of emerging diseases through capacity building in health care preparations, and control reemerging and recurring diseases.",""]],"22":[[1,"92","4","Holistic Health Risk Reduction Programme","Reduce health risk factors in a holistic manner.",""],[1,"92","5","Health Knowledge and Skills Promotion","Knowledge and skills for health care should be provided at the individual, family, and community levels.",""],[1,"92","5","Workplace and Environmental Health Risk Reduction","Health risks at work and in the environment should be reduced.",""],[1,"92","5","Health Early Warning Systems","Warning systems to spot incipient problems should be set to ensure better health.",""],[1,"92","5","Participatory Public Health Policy Formulation","A participatory approach should be promoted to formulate public health policies.",""],[1,"92","5","Herbal Medicine and First Aid Promotion","Use of herbal medicines for disease prevention and knowledge of first aid should be encouraged.",""],[1,"92","5","Digital Health Communication Campaign","Modern communication technology should be used to actively promote health care.",""]],"23":[[1,"32","2","Clean and Alternative Energy Development","The issue of energy security is vital, and requires that more clean energy be used and alternative energy sources be developed, leading to overall improvement in energy efficiency.",""],[1,"99","1","Renewable Biofuel Production Expansion","Governmental policy has also promoted ethanol and biodiesel production in order to reduce imports of fossil fuels.",""],[1,"99","6","Bioenergy and Biogas Production from Solid Waste and Agricultural By-products","Plans should be considered to utilize solid waste and agricultural by products such as paddy husks, corn cover, timber and animal manure to produce bioenergy and biogas and thereby reduce pollution in communities.",""],[1,"100","9","Biofuel Production Expansion","Increase ethanol and biodiesel production by at least 6.2 and 3.6 million liters per day, respectively.",""],[1,"100","9","Renewable Energy Generation from Biomass and Waste","Increase electric power and heat from biomass, biogas and solid wastes from household waste and agricultural and agro-industrial byproducts.",""],[1,"100","9","Energy Efficiency Promotion","Promote energy efficiency widely.",""],[1,"126","4","Renewable Energy Incentive Scheme","Effective incentives should be established to encourage greater use of renewable energy for both electricity and transport needs.",""],[1,"126","4","Biofuel Promotion Initiative","In particular, stimulate the use of biofuel such as gasohol and biodiesel from biomass and solid waste.",""],[1,"126","4","Alternative Energy Information Campaign","Pertinent information should be provided to build a greater understanding of the potential of alternative energy.",""],[1,"126","5","Energy Supply Diversification and Private Sector Investment Support","Provide secure energy and expand its sources of supply by supporting a diversified variety of energy investments and by encouraging the private sector to play a greater role by investing in the energy industry.",""],[1,"126","5","Transparent and Participatory Energy Project Implementation","Popular participation at every stage of implementing energy projects should be achieved through transparency.",""],[1,"127","1","Energy Price Regulation and Monitoring","Monitor energy organizations to ensure stable fair prices for both users and energy providers.",""],[1,"127","2","Renewable Energy Research and Development Support","Promote research and development to replace fossil fuels by producing renewable energy through wind, solar, and water resources.",""],[1,"127","2","Renewable Energy Financing and Infrastructure Support","Meanwhile, distribute financing and infrastructure for research and support that leads to the production of renewable energy that can be commercialized.",""],[1,"127","3","Energy Efficiency Improvement Measures","Measures to conserve energy should be implemented at all levels.",""],[1,"148","3","Renewable Alternative Energy Research and Development Support","An effort is underway to develop alternative energies as a substitute for imports by supporting R&D in renewable, environmentally friendly forms.",""],[1,"160","4","Renewable Energy Tax Incentives and Regulatory Efficiency Reform","Utilize tax support and other incentives to redirect technology and materials toward renewable energy.",""]],"24":[[1,"160","3","Compact Urban Design and Green Infrastructure Development","Develop compact urban designs where areas are used creatively, with emphasis on the expansion of green spaces and increased energy efficiency.",""],[1,"160","3","Infrastructure Design Technology and Transport System Improvement","Infrastructure design technology, improved transport systems and energy saving residential buildings should be promoted.",""],[1,"160","3","Ecologically Sound Urban Model and Urban Agriculture Zones","In addition, an ecologically sound urban model should be developed and specific green areas set aside for agriculture and urban farms.",""],[1,"160","5","Urban Land Use Control and Sprawl Management Measures","Supervise intensive land use both inside and beyond cities and establish measures to curb urban sprawl.",""],[1,"160","5","Public Art and Cultural Heritage Site Designation","Plan to incorporate public art and designate cultural heritage sites.",""],[1,"160","5","Community and Local Administrative Organization Area Development","Communities and LAOs should develop areas at the sub-district, district and provincial levels, and these should be relevant to the means and lifestyle of the inhabitants as well as to the sustainable capacity of these areas.",""],[1,"180","4","Urban Planning and Urban Area Upgrading","Municipalities with high growth potential have applied an \"urban planning\" concept that seeks to upgrade the quality of urban life, enhance facilities for economic and social development within cities and surrounding areas, and promotes balanced development between human and natural resources toward environmental sustainability.",""]],"25":[[1,"27","2","Information Technology for Career Development Access","Information technology should be utilized in parallel with improving access to information for career development.",""],[1,"55","6","Community Wisdom and Learning Infrastructure Development","Infrastructures for sources of wisdom and learning for the community should be provided.",""],[1,"88","6","Lifelong Human Resource Development","Guidelines on human resources in light of global and intra-regional changes, especially those envisioned in the ASEAN Economic Community, should therefore focus on human resource development at all ages within a sustainable lifelong learning social environment.",""],[1,"92","2","Human Resources Development through Lifelong Learning","Develop human resources through a learning process that leads toward a culture of caring and sharing.",""],[1,"92","7","Lifelong Learning Promotion Initiative","Promote lifelong learning.",""],[1,"93","1","Intergenerational and Community Learning Promotion","The habit of learning should be developed from an early stage in life.",""],[1,"93","2","Advanced Alternative Education Promotion","Encourage advanced alternative education consistent with the individual's desires.",""],[1,"93","3","Student-Centered Flexible and Accessible Learning Reform","Arrange learning and its educational processes to have high quality, flexibility, variety, and accessibility.",""],[1,"93","4","Knowledge and Experience Transfer System","Develop a system to transfer knowledge and experience.",""],[1,"93","4","Alternative Education Support Reform","Educational evaluation and further education systems should be adjusted to support alternative education for all groups.",""],[1,"93","5","Online Learning Promotion","3) Promote online learning.",""],[1,"93","5","Tax Incentives for Educational Media Production","Tax incentives should be used to produce educational and learning media as a way to express creative ideas.",""],[1,"93","7","Intellectual Infrastructure Development","Develop intellectual infrastructures at the local, community, and national levels.",""],[1,"93","7","National Broadband and Communication Network Expansion","Communication networks and high speed Internet should be available throughout the country.",""],[1,"93","7","Context-Relevant Learning Resources Development","Learning sources that are consistent with the social landscape should be developed.",""],[1,"93","7","Expansion of Centers of Excellence","Centers of excellence should be expanded to serve regions and local communities.",""],[1,"93","7","Continuous Learning Policy and Regulatory Support","Tax measures, laws and regulations should be used to facilitate continuous learning.",""],[1,"93","8","Community Learning Access and Public Forum Expansion","Increase opportunities for the public and communities to fully utilize available learning sources such as educational institutions, libraries, museums, learning centers, and sport centers.",""],[1,"93","9","Community Knowledge Management and Self-Learning Support","Utilize traditional knowledge and conduct empirical research to foster knowledge management in the community.",""],[1,"94","1","Continuous Learning Opportunities for Out-of-School and Disadvantaged Groups","Create opportunities to learn and develop continuously that are relevant to abilities and environment, especially for children and others outside the formal education system such as student dropouts, children with disabilities, and the underprivileged, as well as people who seek to learn new skills.",""],[1,"94","1","Provincial and Community Stakeholder Coordination for Informal Education","Close cooperation among stakeholders should be formed at the provincial and community levels to target those in the informal education system and to develop an efficient knowledge management system.",""]],"26":[[1,"37","5","Research and Development Enabling Environment","To increase overall productivity and improve the quality of life, research and development should be an important tool for driving the country's development.",""],[1,"37","5","Regulatory Support for Stakeholder Capacity Enhancement","Implementation of appropriate rules and regulations should facilitate better",""],[1,"90","6","Researcher and Innovator Network Expansion","Support the expansion of researchers and innovators, and create networks among them at the domestic and international levels.",""],[1,"90","6","Development of Advanced Innovative Techniques","Advanced innovative techniques should be developed to link modern knowledge with Thai wisdom and culture.",""],[1,"90","6","Creative Economy Development Initiative","Use these links to move toward a creative economy that generates value-added commercial and social goods and services.",""],[1,"90","6","Science, Technology, Arts, and Culture Education Promotion","Emphasis should be placed on knowledge and education in science and technology at the primary through tertiary education levels, and in arts and culture to bring about a creative economy.",""],[1,"103","2","Private Research and Development Support","Support private research and development.",""]],"27":[[1,"24","1","Natural Resource Restoration and Environmental Security Programme","Lastly, restoration of natural resource and environmental capital is focused on community, natural resource and environmental security as well as a low-carbon economy that is environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"26","5","Environmental Quality Improvement and Forest Expansion Initiative","Environmental quality will be improved to meet international standards, reduction of green house gas emissions will be more efficient, and forest areas will be expanded to restore balance to the ecology.",""],[1,"35","2","Forest and Conservation Area Restoration","Conserve and create security for natural resource and environmental bases by safeguarding and restoring forest and conservation areas.",""],[1,"35","2","Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Use Promotion","Encouragement should be given to conservation and to sustainable utilization of biodiversity.",""],[1,"156","3","Forest and Conservation Area Restoration Programme","5.1.1 Restore forest and conservation areas.",""],[1,"156","3","Forest Encroachment Control and Land Demarcation Measures","Curb encroachment on forest areas: register land owners in all conservation areas, define their rights as land owners, and clearly demarcate conservation areas.",""],[1,"156","3","Community Forest Conservation Support Initiative","Civil and community networks for forest conservation and protection should be supported through principles of coexistence between villages and their forests.",""],[1,"156","3","Reforestation of Woodlands Programme","All types of woodlands should be reforested to secure and preserve their benefits.",""],[1,"156","3","Community Forest Management Promotion","Management of community forests should be encouraged, while agroforestry should be restored in the watersheds and along the borderlines of conservation zones.",""],[1,"156","3","Agroforestry Restoration in Watersheds and Conservation Borders","agroforestry should be restored in the watersheds and along the borderlines of conservation zones.",""],[1,"156","4","Database and GIS Development for Land and Natural Resource Management","Develop databases and geographical information systems.",""],[1,"156","5","Land Ownership and Distribution Reform","Reform the overall system of land ownership and distribution to be more equitable.",""]],"28":[[1,"36","2","International Environmental Agreement Review and Negotiation Capacity Building","There is a need to study these agreements in detail to ensure that they are thoroughly understood and to monitor the status of negotiations and the positions of other countries.",""],[1,"36","2","Government Negotiation Skills Development for Environmental Agreements","It is also important that government officials be equipped with negotiation skills and techniques.",""],[1,"36","2","ASEAN and Major Trading Partner Cooperation Enhancement","Moreover, cooperation within ASEAN and with major trading partners should be enhanced.",""],[1,"36","2","Implementation Support for International Natural Resource and Environment Commitments","The implementation of international agreements and commitments on natural resources and environment should be supported.",""],[1,"42","4","Regional Environmental Management Mechanisms","Furthermore, development of mechanisms in other areas such as environmental management at the regional level will lead to a more sustainable use of natural resources in the region.",""],[1,"65","2","Strengthening International Environmental Engagement","The role of the country in international arenas should be strengthened and related to environmental framework agreements and commitments.",""]],"29":[[1,"36","4","Community Empowerment for Natural Resource Access","Support should be given to empower communities and to advocate their rights to gain access and to utilize natural resources.",""],[1,"36","4","Natural Resource Access Legislation Reform","Amendments to legislation are needed to address inequality among communities regarding access to and utilization of natural resources.",""],[1,"36","4","Environmental Investment Policy Reform","Changes in government investment policies to facilitate conservation and restoration are also needed.",""],[1,"36","4","Environmental Tax for Resource Efficiency","An environmental tax should be collected to provide incentives for efficient use of natural resources and pollution reduction.",""],[1,"36","4","Biodiversity Revenue Generation Exploration","Ways and means to generate revenue from biodiversity should be explored.",""],[1,"36","4","Natural Resource Databases and Monitoring Systems","Databases, monitoring and evaluation systems should be developed.",""],[1,"36","4","Natural Resource Management Research Support","Research should be supported to establish an efficient management system for natural resources and the environment.",""],[1,"75","6","Environmental Tax Enforcement Acceleration","Enforcement of environmental taxes should be accelerated to reflect the real costs of production.",""],[1,"167","4","Legal and Regulatory Reform for Equitable Resource Governance","Amend legislation relevant to economic and social changes and enforce laws equitably.",""],[1,"167","5","Government Investment Policy Reform for Natural Resource Conservation","Change government investment policy to promote conservation and restoration of natural resources and the environment.",""],[1,"168","2","Biodiversity-Based Income Generation and Conservation Financing Instruments","Generate income from natural resources and biodiversity conservation.",""],[1,"168","3","Natural Resources and Environment Management Information System","Develop databases, evaluate systems, and support research.",""]],"30":[[1,"160","6","Integrated Urban Wastewater and Solid Waste Management","Manage an integrated urban environment by using innovative technology for wastewater and solid waste management, using the 3R principles (reduce, reuse, and recycle).",""],[1,"160","6","Local Administrative Organization Environmental Management Capacity Building","LAOs should build capacity to manage the environment efficiently with participation by all stakeholders.",""],[1,"165","7","Urban Air Pollution Reduction Measures","Reduce air pollutants, especially particulate matter (PM10).",""],[1,"165","7","Public Transit Expansion and Private Vehicle Reduction","In the big cities, public transit should be provided and people encouraged to avoid using personal vehicles.",""],[1,"165","7","Congestion Charging and Vehicle Use Regulation","Congestion fees should be enacted and use of personal and commercial vehicles should be given an expiration date.",""],[1,"165","7","Urban Planning for Pollution Reduction","Urban planning measures should be strongly applied to reduce traffic, air and noise pollution.",""],[1,"165","7","Public Participation in Development Impact Design","The public should participate in designing measures to prevent harmful effects from development.",""],[1,"165","7","Compensation for Development Damages","When necessary, compensation for damages should be made.",""],[1,"166","1","Open Burning Control by Law","open burning should be controlled by law.",""],[1,"166","2","Solid Waste and Wastewater Efficiency Improvement Measures","Increase efficiency in solid waste disposal and community wastewater treatment.",""]],"31":[[1,"35","2","Integrated Water Resource Management","Integrated water resource management should be urgently pursued.",""],[1,"35","2","Water Resource Restoration and Supply Expansion","In addition, efforts should be made to restore and improve water resources to increase the water supply.",""],[1,"35","2","Water Efficiency Promotion and Water Infrastructure Master Plan","It is essential to promote more efficient use of water.",""],[1,"57","2","Water Resources Development and Restoration","Water resources should be developed, improved or restored to increase the water supply.",""],[1,"57","2","Fair Water Distribution Network and Water Security","Fair water distribution networks and security should be ensured.",""],[1,"57","2","Efficient Water Use Improvement","Water use should be more efficient.",""],[1,"57","2","Agricultural Land Restoration Programme","Exhausted land should be restored and improved for agriculture.",""],[1,"57","2","Protection of Conservation Areas","The problem of invasion of conservation areas should be stopped.",""],[1,"102","5","Fertile Land Restoration and Integrated Water Resource Management","Restoring fertile land, developing integrated water resource management and increasing efficiency in the use of water resources will support productivity in this sector.",""],[1,"154","7","Integrated Water Management Efficiency Improvement","Improve efficiency of the entire water management system to alleviate water shortages, prevent floods, and expand irrigation areas by 200,000 rai per year to increase food security.",""],[1,"157","3","Integrated Water Management Reform","Water management legislation should be amended so that watershed communities and local administrative organizations (LAOs) are empowered to manage river basins.",""],[1,"157","3","River Basin Management Planning","The government should formulate management plans for each river basin using an integrated approach.",""],[1,"157","3","Flood and Drought Risk Management Measures","It should manage critical areas at risk for drought and flood, implement the water grid system, develop a database for water security and forecast equitable water allocation.",""],[1,"157","3","Flood and Drought Disaster Prevention Measures","It should seek to prevent disasters from flood and drought through city plan enforcement, infrastructure improvements, and adaptation of the lifestyle of local people.",""],[1,"157","3","Water Quality Monitoring Partnership","Local administrations, communities, and academia should participate to monitor water quality to meet standards for disease-free drinking water, industrial usage, and ecosystem preservation.",""],[1,"157","4","Water Storage Area Resource Improvement","Improve resources to increase the supply in potential water storage areas.",""],[1,"157","5","Water Allocation System for Agriculture, Industry, and Domestic Consumption","A water allocation system should be established for agriculture, industry and domestic consumption.",""],[1,"158","2","Water Resource Infrastructure Master Plan for Domestic Consumption","Formulate a systematic water resource infrastructure master plan for domestic consumption.",""],[1,"178","3","Water Resources and Land Use Management Programme","7) to manage water resources and land uses to support food security and economic restructuring;",""]],"32":[[1,"126","3","National Water Supply Expansion and Regulation","Enlarge the capability to provide water for consumption, while assuring quality and quantity that meet international standards, and cover both urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"126","3","Water Pricing Regulatory Bodies","Regulatory bodies should be established to set reasonable prices and fees for the water supply.",""],[1,"126","3","Water Consumption Research and Technology Development","Research and technology should be fostered to manage the nation's consumption of water.",""]],"33":[[1,"64","2","Sustainable Agriculture Resource Management Strategy","Emphasis should be placed on managing natural resources to support sustainable agriculture while increasing productivity.",""],[1,"64","2","Agricultural Research and Development Programme","Give high priority to agricultural research and development on flora, fauna and marine species.",""],[1,"64","2","Environmentally Sound Agricultural Technology Promotion","Encourage environmentally sound agricultural technology.",""],[1,"64","2","Agricultural and Food Value Creation Support","Value creation should be given support in agricultural and food products and in energy, and be based on local knowledge and creativity.",""],[1,"64","2","Household, Community, and National Food and Biomass Energy Security","In addition, the establishment of secure food and biomass energy should be emphasized at the household, community and country levels.",""],[1,"102","6","Promotion of Good Agricultural Practices","Regain and encourage good agricultural practices and norms.",""],[1,"102","7","Agricultural Research and Development for Climate-Resilient Species","Emphasize agricultural research and development, especially involving flora and fauna species that are adaptive and able to respond to the impact of climate change.",""],[1,"102","7","Promotion of Improved Flora and Fauna Development","Development of improved flora and fauna should be promoted by using the resources of agricultural institutions, small and micro- community enterprises, community organizations and scholars of local knowledge and farming practices.",""],[1,"102","7","Low-Fossil-Fuel Agricultural Technology Adoption","Fossil fuel use should be reduced by applying agricultural technology.",""],[1,"103","5","Agricultural Tools and Technology Learning Centers","For example, create a center for farming tools and equipment and learning centers for technology development in order to increase production efficiency and the capability to respond to climate change.",""],[1,"103","6","Biodiversity-Supportive Production Promotion","Encourage production that supports basic biodiversity in accordance with climate and environmental conditions.",""],[1,"106","5","Farmer Tree Planting and Community Forestry Promotion","Encourage farmers to plant trees on their own land as well as in community forests.",""],[1,"106","6","Sustainable Agriculture Promotion","Promote sustainable agriculture following the Philosophy.",""],[1,"106","7","Food Knowledge Dissemination and Consumer Awareness Initiative","Encourage dissemination of knowledge and research about food.",""],[1,"107","1","Local Production and Consumption Network Development","Link local production and consumption networks.",""],[1,"107","4","Community Food Security Infrastructure and Management Support","Develop infrastructure and mechanisms to systematically enhance food security in the community.",""],[1,"108","4","Community-Oriented Agricultural Development Support","They should also facilitate agricultural development that meets the needs of local communities and the nation.",""],[1,"156","6","Soil Quality Restoration and Sustainable Agriculture Promotion","Accelerate restoration of soil quality to increase agricultural productivity and food security.",""],[1,"156","6","Sustainable Agriculture System Promotion","A system of sustainable agriculture should be promoted.",""],[1,"157","1","Acidic and Saline Soil Remediation Program","problems of acidic and saline soil should be undertaken;",""],[1,"157","1","Volunteer Soil Doctor Program Support","the work of the Volunteer Soil Doctor program should be encouraged.",""],[1,"157","1","Farmer Soil Conservation Learning Centers","Learning centers for farmers should be set up to help them apply soil conservation technology and restore their lands.",""],[1,"159","2","Sustainable Agriculture Promotion","Organic farming, integrated agriculture, agroforestry, and innovative practices should be promoted in parallel with campaigns to reduce the use of chemicals in agriculture.",""],[1,"159","2","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Technology Development","The development of agricultural technology to adjust land use toward high yield species that use little water and are resistant to climate change is essential.",""],[1,"159","2","Organic Product Market Promotion","Markets for organic products should be promoted.",""],[1,"159","2","Low-Methane Livestock Feeding","Livestock should be fed silage that reduces methane gas;",""],[1,"159","2","Sustainable Fisheries Management Reform","fishing methods should consider the balance between marine animal resources and the eco-system.",""],[1,"159","2","Illegal Fishing Elimination and Fisheries Standards Enforcement","Management of fisheries should observe international standards and include elimination of illegal, unreported and unregulated fishing.",""]],"34":[[1,"104","5","Profitable Aquaculture Development and Cost Reduction","Strengthen and develop profitable aquacultures, and apply technology to reduce production costs.",""],[1,"104","5","Fishery Resource Restoration and Sustainable Management","Fishery resources should be restored and their activities should be managed consistent with the carrying capacity of their natural resource base.",""],[1,"104","5","Illegal Fishing Enforcement and Maritime Resource Protection","Domestic and international legislation should be enforced in order to prevent and eliminate illegal fishing and promote the sustainable use of maritime resources.",""]],"35":[[1,"142","5","Border Area Migration and Trafficking Mitigation Measures","it will be essential to put measures in place to cope with the impact of migrant workers, drug trafficking, and smuggling.",""],[1,"144","7","International Cooperation Against Transnational Threats","Contribute to the international community's efforts in the fight against terrorism, international crimes, drug trafficking, natural disasters and epidemics.",""],[1,"145","1","Border Management and Cross-Border Security Cooperation","Attention should also be paid to improving the system for entering the country, organizing border areas, and resolving problems of the status and rights of foreign workers through cooperation with neighboring countries and the international community.",""]],"36":[[1,"14","4","Regional Interconnectivity and International Cooperation Initiative","Building interconnectivity across countries in the region toward socio-economic security will focus on linking domestic economic expansion to international cooperation.",""],[1,"23","3","Regional and Global Economic Connectivity Enhancement","In the meantime, the nation must increase its connectivity to regional and global economies.",""],[1,"23","3","ASEAN Economic Community Preparedness and Commitment Compliance","To be more proactive with respect to the ASEAN Economy Community (AEC) in 2015, Thailand needs to comply with its commitments under various cooperation frameworks and strengthen its resilience through development of its economic and social capital.",""],[1,"24","1","Enhanced Participation in Global Forums and Trade Resilience","Thailand needs to play a greater role in global forums while resilience in trade, subject to environmental obligations, is enhanced.",""],[1,"31","4","Trade and Investment Reorientation Toward Emerging and Domestic Markets","This strategy should be achieved through adjustment of trends in trade and investment to respond effectively to emerging markets in Asia, the Middle East and Africa, as well as the domestic market.",""],[1,"32","2","Financial and Capital Market Development","The country's competitive edge should be strengthened through development of financial and capital markets along with improvement in the workforce that will facilitate economic restructuring.",""],[1,"32","2","Business Legal and Regulatory Reform","Reform of the legal framework, rules and regulations that govern businesses is also essential in order to bring about healthy competition and enhance efficiency that is capable of meeting global changes and trends.",""],[1,"33","4","ASEAN Economic Community Preparation Measures","Preparations should be made through strengthening public-private cooperation to develop human resources in all economic sectors.",""],[1,"33","5","Regional and International Cooperation Engagement Strategy","Constructively engage in regional and international cooperation frameworks to provide alternatives in foreign policies in the international arena.",""],[1,"33","6","Economic Regional Partnerships for Labor Mobility and Overseas Worker Support","Create economic regional partnerships regarding human capital development and labor migration, and support provisions for Thai laborers in foreign countries.",""],[1,"33","6","Support for Thai Firms Investing Abroad","Support should be given to Thai firms that undertake investment abroad, especially in neighboring",""],[1,"34","3","Constructive International Cooperation for Sustainable Economic Growth","Promote constructive international cooperation to support economic growth in ethical and sustainable ways, including cooperation with non- profit international organizations.",""],[1,"34","4","Free Trade Agreement Utilization Support","Accelerate utilization of free trade agreements currently in effect.",""],[1,"34","4","SME Adaptation and Capacity Support for Free Trade Agreements","the government should support and assist SMEs that are unable to adapt themselves and deal with the aforementioned aspects in a timely manner.",""],[1,"34","5","Support for Regional Operating Headquarters and Non-Profit International Organizations","Benefits and assistance shall be provided for Regional Operating Headquarters (ROHs) and non-profit international organizations in order to increase Thailand's role as a business hub and base for cooperation in the region.",""]],"37":[[1,"133","2","Economic Corridor Connectivity Development","Cooperation objectives will be achieved through the utilization of economic corridors that have the potential to connect GMS countries with one another as well as with the countries in subregional cooperation frameworks beyond ASEAN, such as the Bay of Bengal Initiative on Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC).",""],[1,"133","2","Bay of Bengal Port and Industrial Base Development","BIMSTEC is the product of India's \"look east\" policy, and is manifest in the development of seaports and industrial bases along the Bay of Bengal.",""],[1,"133","2","Myanmar Connectivity Infrastructure Development","These create logistical connections with East Asia as well as infrastructure development to strengthen connectivity with Myanmar.",""],[1,"138","5","Economic Corridor Development and Connectivity Promotion","Utilize international transport infrastructure and the logistics networks among countries that have plans and projects that currently exist, and prepare for those in the future.",""],[1,"139","3","Border Economic Zone and Town Development","Develop economic zones and towns along the border according to the level of mutual benefit and trust with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"139","3","Cross-Border Economic Integration","Economic activities should be integrated with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"139","3","Export Port Infrastructure Development","Port infrastructure for exports will be developed in accordance with present needs and future requirements.",""],[1,"139","3","Equitable Development Partnerships with Neighboring Countries","Thailand will provide support for neighboring countries in the form of equitable development partnerships.",""],[1,"140","2","Regional Supply Chain Interconnection Initiative","Regional supply chains will be interconnected for economic development.",""],[1,"142","2","Border Economic Zone Integration and Coordination Centers","Transport networks that integrate production factors and systems, intercountry value chains, and export gateways should be more efficient.",""],[1,"142","2","Cross-Border Economic Connectivity Network Development","Networks of economic connections should be created among large economic areas in neighboring countries, border areas, and the nation's inland economic zones.",""],[1,"142","2","Thailand-Neighbouring Countries Border Coordination Centers","Coordinating centers among Thailand and neighboring countries should be established in major border cities and towns.",""],[1,"142","3","Mekong Subregion and ASEAN Investment Base Development","Developing investment bases by improving competitiveness in the Mekong subregion and ASEAN.",""],[1,"142","4","Cross-Border Economic Corridor Development","Utilize areas developed to link to neighboring countries and Southeast Asia in order to advance industry, agriculture, agricultural processing, and tourism in the region.",""],[1,"142","4","Public-Private Cross-Border Investment Planning","Moreover, appropriate public agencies should consult with the private sector in drawing up investment plans with public-private participation in neighboring countries .",""],[1,"142","4","Creative Economy and R&D Cooperation with Neighboring Countries","Further, cooperation with neighboring countries should be promoted in the creative areas of the economy, research and development.",""],[1,"142","5","Border Economic Zone Development","Develop economic zones in cities and villages along the border as economic gateways to neighboring countries.",""],[1,"143","2","Cross-Border Spatial Development Planning Integration","Integrate spatial development plans with those of neighboring countries that aim at achieving security and stability in these areas.",""],[1,"146","5","Local Development Coordination Committees","Support local development, especially through committees for integrated management and joint public-private consultative committees at the provincial and regional cluster levels.",""],[1,"146","5","Border Province Development Strategy Coordination","Involve local security agencies in drawing up development strategies, especially for the border provinces.",""],[1,"146","5","Cross-Border Regional Cooperation Framework","The objective is to have a unified vision and be able to develop in a coordinated manner with neighboring countries through cross-border cooperation.",""]],"38":[[1,"132","1","Economic Restructuring for Quality and Sustainable Growth","Thailand finds itself in a situation where there is a need for economic reform through restructuring toward growth that represents quality and is sustainable.",""],[1,"132","1","Regional Economic Integration and Cooperation Strengthening","Cooperation for mutual benefit with ASEAN countries and other neighbors will have to be strengthened with respect to labor, energy, natural resources, production bases, supply chains, goods processing, and logistics systems.",""],[1,"132","1","Regional Financial and Capital Market Expansion","it will be necessary for Thailand to expand its economy by realizing the potential offered from financial and capital markets in this region.",""],[1,"132","2","International Connectivity and Economic Integration Efforts","during the Eleventh Plan, Thailand will have to put forth efforts to create and strengthen connectivity with countries in various regions in order to prepare for changes and maintain the country's economic and social security.",""],[1,"132","2","Domestic-Regional Economic Linkage Development","Moreover, links connecting the domestic and regional economies will be essential and take into",""],[1,"134","2","Implementation of the Master Plan on ASEAN Connectivity","Implementation of the Master Plan on ASEAN Connectivity will have a vital role in creating links within ASEAN in terms of infrastructure, laws and regulations, and person-to-person contact.",""],[1,"134","3","ASEAN Competitiveness Preparation and Enterprise Capacity Strengthening","To achieve this goal, Thailand will have to accelerate its preparations for free competition within the ASEAN community.",""],[1,"135","3","APEC Framework Utilization","The long- established APEC framework would also continue to be utilized.",""],[1,"140","1","Regional and Multilateral Cooperation Promotion","To promote Thailand as a key actor in cooperation under various frameworks that include subregional areas, ASEAN, the ASEAN Plus alliances and the Asia-Pacific region.",""],[1,"140","11","Implementation of the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan","the formation of the ASEAN Community in 2015 will have to be fully realized through implementation of the Master Plan on ASEAN Connectivity.",""],[1,"141","1","Subregional Trade and Investment Connectivity Expansion","This will lead to an expansion in trade and investment within and between subregions and ASEAN.",""],[1,"141","1","Asia-Pacific Cooperation Expansion","The potential benefits of connecting with nearby subregions and the expansion in cooperation with other frameworks in the Asia-Pacific region will also have to be exploited.",""],[1,"143","6","Regional and International Cooperation Engagement Framework","Constructively engage in frameworks for regional and international cooperation to provide alternatives in foreign policy in the international arena that maintain benefits for the nation.",""],[1,"143","7","Regional Economic Cooperation Strategy Formulation","Assume an active role in formulating strategies that involve appropriate structures of cooperation such as APEC and the East Asia Summit.",""],[1,"144","1","Monitoring and Evaluation of Emerging Cooperation Framework Participation","monitor and evaluate the advantages of joining emerging cooperation frameworks such as the Asia-Middle East Dialogue (AMED) and Trans- Pacific Partnership (TPP).",""],[1,"144","3","Regional Economic Partnerships for Human Capital and Labor Mobility","Create regional economic partnerships on human capital development and labor mobility, and provide support for Thai labor working abroad via a linkage of supply chains and free labor mobility.",""],[1,"146","2","Support for Non-Profit International Organizations in Thailand","Promote and assist non-profit international organizations to assume greater roles in using Thailand as an operational base for development in this region.",""],[1,"146","3","Community-Level Domestic Development Partner Strengthening","Strengthen domestic development partners at the community level to prepare to join global development initiatives.",""],[1,"146","6","Technical Capacity and Academic Network Support","Provide support for enhancing technical capacity and for networks of Thai academic institutions in order to create close collaboration with other countries in this region.",""]],"39":[[1,"29","2","Health Risk Reduction and Public Health Service Improvement","Encourage the reduction of risk factors in health.",""],[1,"29","2","Health Literacy and Community Health Knowledge Programme","Citizens should also possess knowledge and skills in health care at the individual, family and community levels.",""],[1,"29","2","Public Health Policy Participation Mechanism","They should participate in formulating public policies regarding health care.",""],[1,"29","2","Public Health Service Quality and Coverage Improvement","Public health services should be improved through better quality and coverage, and promote the use of alternative medicines.",""],[1,"29","2","Equitable Redistribution of Health Personnel","The supply of health personnel should be redistributed more equitably and a national health database should be created.",""],[1,"29","2","National Health Database Development","a national health database should be created.",""],[1,"29","2","Efficient and Sustainable Health Financing Management","Monetary and fiscal measures for health care should be managed in an efficient and sustainable manner.",""]],"40":[[1,"126","2","National ICT Infrastructure Modernization","Modernize the information and communication technology (IT) infrastructure so it provides high-speed data transmission and internet connection covering all areas in the country.",""],[1,"126","2","E-Government Service Development","E-government services should be created through high-speed communication networks for education, public health, and agriculture.",""],[1,"126","2","Digital Inclusion and SME ICT Adoption Promotion","Both citizens and small and medium businesses should be encouraged to use high speed telecommunication and information technology to enhance the quality of life and generate income.",""],[1,"126","2","IT Human Resource Development Plan","Human resource development plans for IT should be formulated for the country's long-term growth.",""],[1,"126","2","Creative Economy Digital Content Development","Applications and content associated with the expansion of a creative economy should be developed.",""],[1,"128","1","Communication and Telecommunications Regulatory Revision","Revise rules and regulations in the communication and telecommunication sectors.",""]],"41":[[1,"122","1","Technology and Innovation Promotion for Business Matching","technology and innovation should be encouraged.",""],[1,"122","1","Business Matching for Technology-Based Strengthening","Businesses should be matched in order to develop their strength, based on technology and innovation.",""],[1,"122","2","Science, Technology, Research and Innovation Development Initiative","Develop science, technology, research and innovation as driving forces for inclusive growth.",""],[1,"122","3","Science, Technology, Research and Innovation Enabling Environment","Create an environment that enables development and application of science, technology, research and innovation to promote creativity and added value in the production sector.",""],[1,"122","4","Joint Venture Incentives and PPP Research Fund","Increase monetary, financial and other incentives to encourage joint ventures and set up a public-private partnership research fund.",""],[1,"122","4","Research and Development Regulatory Reform","Laws and regulations that are obstacles should be revised so they do not hinder the application of research and development.",""],[1,"122","4","Government Procurement Support for Research and Development","Government procurement mechanisms should be used to support research and development.",""],[1,"122","4","Technology-Based Product Demand Creation","Demand for technology-based products should be created.",""],[1,"122","5","National Research and Development Support Measures","Design measures to support national research and development projects and technology transfer through foreign direct investment.",""],[1,"122","5","International Standards for Animal Use in Scientific Studies","The use of animals in scientific studies should meet international standards.",""],[1,"122","6","Science, Technology, Research and Innovation Coordination and Evaluation System","Improve the efficiency of science, technology, research and innovation management by establishing a coordinating system among relevant agencies at the policy and implementation levels as well as providing for an effective and transparent evaluation and follow-up system.",""],[1,"122","7","Science, Technology, Research and Innovation Infrastructure Development","Develop infrastructure that facilitates science, technology, research and innovation in both quality and quantity through public and private partnership as follows:",""],[1,"122","8","Science Park and Research Center Development","Accelerate development of science parks, intelligence centers, incubation centers, research and development institutes, specialized science research institutes and testing centers to satisfy existing demand, especially at the regional level.",""],[1,"122","8","Private and Foreign Investment in Research Centers","the private sector and foreign investors should support the establishment of research centers in Thailand.",""],[1,"122","8","Geospatial Data Integration in Development Planning","Also, geographical data should figure in the country's development planning.",""],[1,"122","9","Research and Innovation Collaborative Networks","Encourage investment in research and innovation through collaborative networks among academic institutes, research institutes, the production sector, communities, clusters, and associations within and outside the",""],[1,"123","1","Joint Research Program Development and Knowledge Sharing Mechanism","country to conduct joint research programs and transfer and share knowledge in order to generate benefits and manage risks.",""],[1,"123","2","On-the-Job Scientist Training and Scholarship Support","Develop scientists through on-the-job training.",""],[1,"123","2","Science-Based Public Awareness and Knowledge Access Expansion","Thai people should be encouraged to think and act based on facts and scientific evidence.",""],[1,"178","3","Economic Restructuring Facilities Upgrade","4) to upgrade facilities for economic restructuring to increase competitiveness and fairness;",""],[1,"181","4","Integrated Research and Development for National Development","Government agencies that make policy should integrate their work and utilize research and development (R&D) resources, which they will apply as tools for progress.",""],[1,"181","4","Research Agency Cooperation Network","Cooperation by research agencies will be advocated, especially networks of (a) the National Research Council of Thailand (NRCT), (b) the Thailand Research Fund (TRF), (c) the National Science and Technology Development Agency (NSTDA), (e) the National Science Technology and Innovation Policy Office (STI), (f) the Health Systems Research Institute (HSRI), and (g) the Agricultural Research Development Agency (ARDA).",""],[1,"181","4","Local R&D Coordination through Regional Science Parks","Also, academic institutions such as the Regional Science Park should coordinate R&D at the local level, especially when high-priority development is undertaken.",""],[1,"181","5","National Science, Technology and Innovation Framework","the First National Policy and Plan for Science, Technology and Innovation (2012-2021) as a framework for efficient development",""]],"42":[[1,"159","1","Private Sector Social Responsibility Incentives","Incentives should be provided to encourage the private sector to accept social responsibility and to facilitate joint investments between them and the local communities.",""],[1,"159","1","Social Enterprise Awareness Dissemination","At the same time, the concept of social enterprise should be disseminated among development partners.",""]],"43":[[1,"78","1","Local Community Capacity Strengthening and Decentralized Governance","Strengthen the capacity of local communities to manage their own problems efficiently.",""],[1,"78","4","Community Empowerment Support","Community empowerment should be supported.",""],[1,"78","4","Transparent and Efficient Local Administrative Capacity Development","Local administrative bodies should be developed to translate development strategies into action that is transparent and efficient at the local level.",""],[1,"94","8","Participatory Community Development Support","Support a participatory approach to developing the community, based on the principle of self- reliance according to its potential, natural resources, wisdom, lifestyle, culture, and environment.",""],[1,"95","2","Intergenerational Capacity Building and Community Cooperation Networks","Extend successes and promote capacity building among three generations in order to create mutual understanding toward a better quality of life in the family and community.",""]],"44":[[1,"76","5","Low-Income Housing and Livable City Policy","Draft a national habitat and livable city policy, develop housing projects, and solve the problem of urban slums through cooperation with the private sector.",""],[1,"76","5","Private Sector Social Assistance Expansion","Also, the private sector role in providing social assistance should be enhanced.",""]],"45":[[1,"94","4","Family Capacity Enhancement for Employment and Income Security","Enhance family capacity for securing employment and income to ensure self-sufficiency.",""],[1,"94","4","Family Learning and Intergenerational Knowledge Transfer Support","An appropriate learning process should be supported relevant to the family's potential.",""],[1,"94","4","Family Relationship Incentives and Digital Communication Skills Support","Rewards should be given to families with good relationships.",""],[1,"94","4","Parent and Guardian Communications Technology Capacity Building","Parents and guardians should be equipped with knowledge of communications technology, and provided with access to efficient use of it to enhance family relationships.",""]],"46":[[1,"89","4","Pre-Primary Child Development Promotion","Promote the development of children at the pre-primary level in all aspects, including intelligence, emotion, morality, and integrity.",""],[1,"89","5","Parent and Guardian Child Development Support","Prepare parents and guardians to take care of children in a way that is appropriate to their mental, intellectual, and physical development.",""],[1,"89","5","Happy Learning Environment Promotion","A happy learning environment should be created by encouraging critical thinking, experimentation, and adaptation of knowledge acquired in class to real life situations.",""],[1,"89","5","Parent Role Model Development for Child Ethics","Parents should be encouraged to serve as role models for children in ethics, morality, and integrity.",""],[1,"89","6","Childcare Center Quality Improvement Programme","Improve the quality of childcare centers in the community, in firms and in government agencies to meet the standards that are relevant to each social landscape.",""]],"47":[[1,"56","1","Universal Social Protection System Development","A high quality social protection system that covers the entire populace should be encouraged.",""],[1,"73","6","High-Quality Social Protection Coverage","Citizens will be covered by a high quality social protection system.",""],[1,"76","2","Expanded Social Protection Coverage","Enhance social protection to cover people at all levels consistent with their needs.",""],[1,"76","2","Equal Social Security for Formal and Informal Workers","Social security should be provided with equality and fairness for workers in both the formal and informal sectors.",""],[1,"76","2","Labor Welfare Support Programme","Labor welfare should be given support to strengthen the quality of life.",""],[1,"76","2","Integrated Social Protection Database Linkage","Databases should be connected efficiently to ensure higher quality social protection.",""],[1,"76","6","National and Community Social Welfare System Linkage","Improve social welfare systems from birth to death by linking the national and community levels.",""],[1,"77","3","Social Protection Database Development","Develop a database to ensure coverage and effectiveness of social protection.",""],[1,"77","3","Analytical Capacity Building for Social Protection Programming","In addition, improvement of analytical and synthesizing skills is required to develop needed programs that assist target groups in gaining access to efficient services.",""]],"48":[[1,"91","7","Older Persons Income and Employment Support Measures","Promote measures to generate income and employment opportunities for older persons by identifying jobs and wage rates appropriate to their situation.",""],[1,"91","7","Skills and Self-Improvement Training for Older Persons","They should be provided with academic skills and the capacity for work and self-improvement.",""],[1,"91","7","Digital Learning Support for Older Persons","Modern communication technology should be utilized to help them learn.",""],[1,"91","8","National Brain Bank Knowledge Utilization Initiative","Utilize more fully the particular knowledge and wisdom of those individuals registered in the National Brain Bank (2000), and seek to use local wisdom in rural areas, communities, and in the country at large for development.",""],[1,"92","1","Elderly Self-Reliance Support and Age-Friendly Environment Programme","Increase the ability of the elderly to be self-reliant.",""],[1,"92","1","Age-Friendly Physical Environment Modification","Their physical environment should be modified to better serve their age group.",""],[1,"92","1","Integrated Health Care and Social Welfare System Development","A variety of health care and social welfare systems should be developed in a holistic manner with the participation of every sector.",""],[1,"92","1","Community-Based Elderly Care Model Expansion","Successful community models for the care of older persons should be extended to other communities.",""]],"49":[[1,"13","4","Strengthening Economic and Social Security","The promotion of social equality will focus on strengthening economic and social security so that everyone in Thai society has access to quality services, resources, and basic infrastructure that are essential for starting a career and maintaining a stable income.",""],[1,"13","4","Equal Access to Justice and Public Services","This will include equal access to the judicial system, and the ability to enjoy life with dignity under a government that respects transparency, the common public interest, and opportunity for people from all sectors to be engaged in the development process.",""],[1,"24","1","Social Capital Empowerment for Human and Social Development","First, empowerment of social capital - human, social and cultural - concentrates on human and social development toward a quality society.",""],[1,"27","2","Tax System Restructuring for Fairer Resource Allocation","Allocation of resources should be made more just by restructuring the tax system to improve income distribution and serve as a tool for fair allocation of resources and ownership of property.",""],[1,"27","2","Expanded Social Protection Coverage","the private sector should play a greater role in enhancing socio-economic security for all citizens, and social protection should be upgraded and cover all people.",""],[1,"27","3","Social Service Access and Quality Improvement","The quality of public services should be improved, and access to such services should be increased, particularly housing and public utilities for low income groups.",""],[1,"27","3","Social Welfare Upgrade Programme","Social welfare should be upgraded to a standard of high quality and efficiency.",""],[1,"27","3","Community Grassroots Finance and Savings Mobilization","At the community level, grass- roots finance and various types of saving should be improved so resources can be mobilized.",""],[1,"27","3","Social Protection Database System","A database system should be developed to ensure the coverage and effectiveness of social protection in accordance with basic rights.",""],[1,"28","1","Promotion of Occupational Groups","The formation of occupational groups should be promoted and based on the potentials of the various communities.",""],[1,"28","1","Multi-Stakeholder Social Development Coordination","The roles played by the private sector, civil society, and local government should be synergized in the development of society.",""],[1,"28","1","Consumer Protection Improvement","Consumer protection should be improved to meet high standards.",""],[1,"28","1","Consumer Rights Information Access Expansion","There should be increasing access to information and knowledge about rights and the protection of consumers.",""],[1,"178","3","Economic and Social Security Enhancement Programme","2) to enhance economic and social security in the society;",""]],"50":[[1,"77","1","Grassroots Finance and Savings Institution Development","Improve and diversify grassroots finance and savings institutions.",""]],"51":[[1,"27","3","Gender Equality Attitude Promotion","Positive attitudes toward gender equality should be encouraged in order to increase participation in decision making.",""],[1,"28","1","Women’s Leadership Promotion","Women should be promoted to managerial and decision-making positions at both local and national levels to add a greater contribution to the country's development.",""],[1,"73","6","Women’s Economic and Leadership Advancement","Women will have a better likelihood of attaining a higher income and promotion to executive and decision-making levels leading to greater gender equality.",""],[1,"75","5","Capacity Building and Awareness Support for Women, Older Persons, and Persons with Disabilities","In addition, opportunities and capacity building for women, older persons, and the disabled should be supported; this would include raising awareness of the responsibilities of consumers, communities and society toward them.",""],[1,"77","2","Gender Equality Attitudes and Awareness Promotion","Enhance attitudes toward gender equality in children, youth, and the populace.",""],[1,"77","2","Institutional Cooperation for Gender Equality Values","Cooperation is needed among institutions, particularly the family, educational and religious institutions and the media, to foster values and attitudes of gender equality.",""],[1,"77","2","Violence Against Women Eradication Initiative","Violence against women should be eradicated.",""],[1,"77","2","Women’s Career Advancement and Leadership Promotion","More opportunities should be given to women for career advancement toward managerial and decision- making positions at both local and national levels in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"77","2","Women’s Empowerment and Participation Strengthening","This can be accomplished by strengthening the potential of women and expanding the perceptions of the populace in various areas, for example, knowledge, understanding, awareness, ideology, values, ethics, democratic culture, and good governance.",""],[1,"79","2","Women’s Leadership and Gender Equality Promotion Measures","Increase the role of women in management and decision making positions at both local and national levels to support the country's development.",""]],"52":[[1,"80","5","Legal Assistance and Expanded Legal Services Program","Encourage fairness in the judicial system, create a strong legal assistance program, and expand legal services.",""],[1,"80","5","Community Justice Network Strengthening","Intensify efforts to strengthen community justice networks where conflicts can be managed within the community.",""],[1,"80","5","Legal Rights Awareness and Know-the-Law Campaigns","people should be encouraged to broaden their knowledge regarding their rights and duties, and have easier access to the judicial system.",""],[1,"80","5","Legal Status and Registration System Improvement","Legal status and registration systems should be improved.",""]],"53":[[1,"30","3","Farmer Income and Crop Insurance System","An income insurance system, together with crop insurance, should be developed to cover all farmers.",""],[1,"30","3","Fair Contract Farming Framework","Fairness for farmers and stakeholders in the contract farming system should be encouraged.",""],[1,"30","3","Agricultural Self-Reliance Support through Institutes and Community Enterprises","Agricultural institutes and community enterprises should be major mechanisms for supporting self- reliance.",""],[1,"30","3","Support for Small Farmers Affected by Free Trade Agreements","At the same time, small farmers adversely affected by free trade agreements should be strengthened in order to maintain their living conditions.",""],[1,"30","4","Household and Community Food Security and Bio-energy Initiative","Enhance food security and develop bio-energy at household and community levels.",""],[1,"105","5","Farmer Income Insurance System","Develop an income insurance system that covers all farmers.",""]],"54":[[1,"28","3","Population Distribution and Fertility Management","Adjust the population structure and its distribution to be appropriate.",""]],"55":[[1,"57","3","Greenhouse Gas Reduction Research and Innovation","Research and development, innovation on greenhouse gas reduction, and preparation for greenhouse effects should be encouraged.",""],[1,"61","7","Economic Restructuring for Environmental Sustainability","To enhance production and services through greater efficiency, through knowledge, innovation, creativity, and folk wisdom, and to develop food and energy security, restructure the economy and consumption practices to be environmentally healthy, and to strengthen international cooperation with neighboring countries for economic and social security.",""],[1,"61","8","Natural Resource and Environmental Security Programme","To build a secure base of natural resources and a sound environment, support community participation, and safeguard people and the nation from the effects of climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"62","8","Environmental Quality Improvement and Forest Expansion","Environmental quality will be improved to meet international standards, reduction of greenhouse gas emissions will be efficiently achieved, and forest areas will be expanded for ecological balance.",""],[1,"65","2","Low-Carbon Economy and Society Transition","The development paradigm should be shifted toward an environmentally safe low-carbon economy and society.",""]],"56":[[1,"27","1","Environmentally Friendly Production and Consumption Promotion","To create and utilize economic opportunities, knowledge, technology and creativity will be crucial factors for environmentally friendly production and consumption leading to sustainable development.",""],[1,"36","1","Trade Resilience and Environmental Monitoring Measures","Efforts should be made for surveillance and monitoring measures that are related to environmental conservation and that may have effects on international trade and investment.",""]],"57":[[1,"161","7","Climate Change Research and Sectoral Risk Assessment","Conduct research for better precision about the causes, forecasting, risk assessment, vulnerability, and impacts from climate change on each sector of the economy and society.",""],[1,"161","8","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Research and Innovation Support","Support scientific and technological research and innovation regarding adaptation to greenhouse gas emissions and their reduction.",""],[1,"161","8","Domestic Carbon Market Preparation Study","In addition, studies should be undertaken about the preparation of the domestic carbon market; mitigation in the energy and agriculture sectors; new mechanisms such as the National Appropriation Mitigation Action (NAMA); Reducing Emission from Deforestation and Degradation and the Role of Forest Carbon Stocks in Developing Countries (REDD-Plus); and Clean Development Mechanisms (CDMs).",""],[1,"161","9","Climate Change Curriculum Development for Researchers","Develop a curriculum on climate change to train researchers and create and participate in information networks.",""],[1,"162","1","Climate Change Data Evaluation and Information Dissemination Mechanism","Establish mechanisms to evaluate data and disseminate climate change information to all sectors in order to raise public awareness and alleviate its impacts.",""],[1,"162","3","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Database and Reporting System","Develop databases and reporting systems to measure greenhouse gas emissions.",""],[1,"162","4","Innovative Technology Development","Development of innovative technology is also essential.",""],[1,"162","5","Greenhouse Gas Mitigation Planning and MRV System","Set targets for greenhouse gas reduction and formulate medium- and long-term action plans for voluntary mitigation of greenhouse gases by promoting its benefits.",""],[1,"162","6","Carbon Credit Market Research and Emissions Trading Studies","Conduct market research to identify revenue opportunities through selling carbon credits, including standards that link to international markets on both a voluntary and a regulated basis.",""],[1,"162","7","National Registry System for Greenhouse Gas Reduction","Establish a National Registry System to bolster domestic greenhouse gas reduction including reports on NAMA activities.",""],[1,"162","7","Regulatory Amendments for Climate Finance and Carbon Market Support","Regulations should be amended to gain international support relative to finance, technology, capacity building and establishment of a Thai carbon market in the future.",""],[1,"163","1","Carbon Fund for Carbon Credits and Offsets","Establish a carbon fund as a domestic buying source for carbon credits and offsets.",""],[1,"163","1","ASEAN Carbon Market Feasibility Study","A feasibility study should be supported on establishing a carbon market for the ASEAN Economic Community (AEC).",""]],"58":[[1,"36","3","Air Pollution Reduction Measures","Control and reduce pollution.",""],[1,"36","3","Solid Waste Disposal and Community Wastewater Treatment Improvement","The efficiency of solid waste disposal and community waste water treatment should be improved.",""],[1,"36","3","Hazardous, Electronic, and Infected Waste Management System","a management system for hazardous, electronic and infected wastes should be established.",""],[1,"36","3","Toxic Accident Warning and Response Systems","Development of warning systems and responses for toxic accidents are needed.",""],[1,"65","2","Pollution Reduction through Improved Control Management","Pollution reduction should be achieved by improving management of controls.",""]],"59":[[1,"159","5","Public Transportation Network Development for Energy Efficiency","Public transportation networks should be developed to reduce energy use in order to attain greater efficiency throughout the country.",""],[1,"160","1","Clean and Renewable Vehicle Promotion","Support the use of vehicles that use clean or renewable energy such as natural gas and biofuel.",""],[1,"160","1","Energy-Saving Automobile Technology Development","Automobile technology that saves energy together with productivity enhancement should be developed.",""],[1,"160","1","Fuel Consumption Standards","Fuel consumption standards should be set to compel reduced use; this will be the main mechanism to control greenhouse gas emissions in the long term.",""],[1,"160","2","Road Safety and Vehicle Emissions Control Measures","Poor driving behavior and excessive speed should be curtailed to reduce fuel consumption.",""]],"60":[[1,"65","2","Public Participation in Natural Resource Protection and Conservation","This will place the emphasis on maintaining balance within the ecosystem through public participation in protection, conservation and utilization.",""],[1,"65","2","Natural Resource Conservation, Restoration, and Protection","Natural resources and the environmental base should be conserved, restored and secured.",""],[1,"65","2","Environmental Management System Efficiency and Transparency Reform","Natural resource and environmental management systems should become more efficient, transparent and equitable.",""],[1,"65","2","Protection of Trade from Environmental and Climate Shocks","International trade should be protected from crises that result from environmental conditions and climate change.",""],[1,"153","6","Integrated Area-Based Natural Resource Management","Emphasis should be placed on an integrated area-based approach that aims to improve management mechanisms.",""],[1,"153","6","Environmental Management Database Development","Databases should be developed to support",""],[1,"154","6","Natural Resource and Biodiversity Conservation Expansion","Enrich the abundance of natural resources and biodiversity so that conservation lands occupy at least 19 percent of total area, expand forest reserves up to 40 percent, and attain at least 5,000 rai per year of mangrove coastal reforestation.",""],[1,"155","9","Natural Resource and Environmental Restoration and Conservation","the development strategies during the Eleventh National Economic and Social Development Plan should emphasize (1) restoration and conservation of natural resources and the environment",""],[1,"156","1","Natural Resource and Environment Management System Development","(6) development of the natural resource and environment management system so that it is efficient, transparent and equitable;",""],[1,"157","2","Marine and Coastal Resources Management System","Establish a management system for marine and coastal resources.",""],[1,"157","2","Mangrove Reforestation and Coastal Ecosystem Rehabilitation","The government should alleviate the impact of major natural disasters and coastal erosion by promoting mangrove reforestation, coral reef rehabilitation, and sea grass and seaweed conservation.",""]],"61":[[1,"154","8","Environmental Pollution Reduction and Water Quality Regulation","Create a more pleasant environment by reducing the pollution and threats to health from development.",""],[1,"155","9","Pollution Reduction for Public Health","pollution reduction to ensure better health for the population",""]],"62":[[1,"158","3","Biodiversity Conservation and Equitable Benefit-Sharing Measures","Encourage conservation and share the benefits of biodiversity equitably.",""],[1,"158","3","Protection of Conservation Areas and Vulnerable Ecosystems","Conservation areas and vulnerable ecosystems should be protected to preserve biodiversity.",""],[1,"158","3","Community-Based Local Species Conservation Support","Community organizations should be encouraged to conserve local species.",""],[1,"158","3","Regulatory Reform for Access to Biological Resources","Regulations should be amended to facilitate access to biological resources for food security in the community.",""],[1,"158","3","Value-Added Innovation from Biological Resources","Value added innovations should be generated from biological resources.",""],[1,"165","5","Biodiversity Convention Implementation Measures","To implement the Convention on Biodiversity and its related protocols, there are several important policies to consider.",""]],"63":[[1,"118","2","Ecologically Sound and Community-Friendly Investment Promotion","Promote sustainable enterprises and achieve balanced development in economic, social, and environmental dimensions by focusing on ecologically sound and community-friendly investment.",""],[1,"118","2","High-Tech Low-Carbon Industry Investment Incentives","The emphasis should be to induce investment in industries that utilize advanced knowledge, high technology, and low carbon production.",""],[1,"121","2","Eco-Industrial Town Development and Environmental Restoration","Develop eco-industrial towns and restore the environment in major industrial regions by creating awareness of the need for coexistence between industries and communities.",""],[1,"127","5","Ecotown, Ecozone, and Eco-Industrial Estate Development","The development of ecotowns, ecozones and eco-industrial estates should be promoted.",""],[1,"145","5","Green Production, Consumption and Services Promotion","Promote green production, consumption and services that lead to reduction of GHG emissions, pollution, inefficient use of natural resources, and environmental impacts.",""],[1,"152","5","Greenhouse Gas Mitigation Preparedness","Thailand must be prepared to take responsibility for greenhouse gas mitigation in the future.",""],[1,"152","5","Cleaner Production Adjustment Across Sectors","All production sectors, including agriculture, industry and services will have to adjust their processes to be less environmentally harmful in response to international requirements and bilateral agreements with the country's trade partners.",""],[1,"155","9","Green Economy Transition and Environmentally Friendly Society","a shift in the development paradigm and a transition to a green economy and a society that is environmentally friendly",""],[1,"158","5","Industrial Green Technology Upgrade Support","Upgrade industries that have emitted high levels of greenhouse gases toward environmentally safe technology by providing low-interest loans and tax incentives to retrofit machinery, increase efficiency, and switch from fossil fuels to renewable energy.",""],[1,"158","6","Low-Carbon Industrial Promotion Policy Revision","Revise industrial promotion policies to provide more benefits for low-carbon industries and those that are reducing carbon, and halt investments by transnational industries that create harmful environmental effects.",""],[1,"158","7","Domestic Mitigation Mechanisms for Sustainable Development","Accelerate domestic mitigation mechanisms that foster sustainable development and respond to international standards.",""],[1,"158","8","Eco-Industrial Town Development","Encourage coexistence of industries with communities through eco-industrial towns where most wastes can be recycled and raw materials managed systematically.",""],[1,"158","8","Eco-Industrial Area Community Engagement","Communicate with all parties to create understanding of the benefits of eco-industrial area development in order to change community attitudes prior to the",""]],"64":[[1,"92","3","Social Responsibility and Environmental Awareness Campaign","Instill the value of social responsibility in the population.",""],[1,"160","8","Public Environmental Awareness and Ecosystem Stewardship Campaign","Encourage people from all sectors to be responsible for their ecosystems by applying the Philosophy to their way of life in order that Thailand becomes a model of an environmentally sustainable society.",""],[1,"160","8","Public Education on Natural Resource and Environmental Sustainability","Educate the public to be aware of the concept that natural resources and the environment are vital to survival and the progress of human society.",""]],"65":[[1,"24","1","National Resilience and Balanced Development Strategy","Development is intended to generate resilience in every dimension of Thailand's progress toward balance and sustainability by strengthening and utilizing its capital endowment.",""],[1,"24","1","National Preparedness for Climate Change and Natural Disasters","National preparedness is designed to cope with effects from climate change and natural disasters.",""],[1,"27","1","Development Strategy Formulation for Risk Management","In dealing with rapid changes and complicated and unpredictable environmental events, a set of development strategies will be formulated for better risk management and to create a firm foundation for development.",""],[1,"34","2","Regional Disaster and Emergency Preparedness Cooperation","There is also a need for capacity improvement and enhanced regional cooperation in dealing with natural disasters and emergencies, and in collaborating in the prevention of infection and the spread of emerging and re-emerging diseases.",""],[1,"35","4","Climate Change Adaptation Capacity Upgrade","Upgrade the ability to adapt to climate change.",""],[1,"35","5","National Disaster Preparedness and Response Planning","Maps and priority lists of risk areas should be prepared at the national, regional and provincial levels.",""],[1,"35","5","Disaster Management Efficiency Improvement","Disaster management efficiency should be improved while database systems and telecommunication networks should be developed.",""],[1,"35","5","Disaster Management Science and Technology Support","Support is also needed to provide for the development of science and technology in disaster management.",""],[1,"35","5","National Volunteer Disaster Response System Upgrade","The national volunteer work system should be improved to meet international standards.",""],[1,"35","5","Multi-Stakeholder Disaster Response Action Planning","Moreover, the private sector, enterprises, schools and local authorities should be well prepared with action plans for disaster response.",""],[1,"163","5","National, Regional, and Provincial Risk Mapping and Prevention Planning","Map risk areas at the national, regional and provincial levels.",""],[1,"163","5","Risk-Zone Surveillance and Damage Prevention Guidelines","Set priorities to determine guidelines for surveillance and damage prevention using physical measurements and infrastructures.",""],[1,"163","5","Control of Economic Activities and Settlements in Risk Zones","Control both economic activities and settlements in risk zones.",""],[1,"163","5","Safety Standards for Utilities and Key Infrastructure","Safety standards for utilities and other key infrastructures should be defined to handle future disasters.",""],[1,"163","6","Disaster Management Efficiency Upgrade","Upgrade the efficiency of disaster management.",""],[1,"163","7","Disaster Management Databases and Telecommunications System","Develop databases and a telecommunication system.",""],[1,"163","7","Regional Disaster Management Knowledge Network","A regional network should be created to link data, transfer technology, encourage academic collaboration, and in general create knowledge about warning systems and emergency management.",""],[1,"163","8","National Disaster Relief Planning","Establish disaster relief planning for the entire population.",""],[1,"163","8","National Volunteer Corps Establishment","A national volunteer corps should be created to meet international standards.",""],[1,"163","8","Community Disaster Management Capacity Building","Capacity development for communities and local leaders should be supported both through training and by disseminating information about disaster management.",""],[1,"164","1","National Disaster Management Resource Mobilization and Integration","among sectors, both government and private, should be a high priority, and include academia, mass media, the military, and civil society to efficiently mobilize resources and integrate disaster management throughout the country.",""],[1,"164","2","Disaster Response Planning and Emergency Drill Programme","Disaster response plans should be made to carry out actions such as evacuation.",""],[1,"164","2","Organizational Business Continuity Backup System","There should be a back-up system of operation at the organization level to ensure business continuity.",""],[1,"178","3","Disaster Management and Climate Change Preparedness Programme","8) to develop disaster management to cope with climate changes;",""]],"66":[[1,"33","3","Integrated Spatial Development Plan for Regional Connectivity","This should be achieved through spatial development that improves connectivity with neighboring countries and South-East Asia, and is based on an integrated spatial development plan for mutual security and stability.",""],[1,"35","3","Eco-City Development Initiative","Eco-cities should be developed that emphasize urban planning and integration of cultural, social and ecological factors.",""]],"67":[[1,"145","2","Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Capacity Improvement","Prepare for natural disasters and emergencies through improvements in capacity and through regional cooperation in disaster management using business contingency plans.",""],[1,"145","2","Public-Private ICT Partnership for Business Continuity and Protection","A public-private relationship should be created to protect business, trade, and human life, while sustaining economic growth and a high quality of life through effective information and communication technology.",""],[1,"154","9","Climate Change and Disaster Adaptive Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the adaptive capacity to meet climate change challenges and disasters at all levels - community, regional, and countrywide.",""],[1,"155","6","Climate Change Management Mechanisms","Mechanisms to manage climate change; databases showing areas at risk from climate change at national, regional, and provincial levels; surveillance and early warning systems in the areas most likely to experience natural disasters.",""],[1,"155","9","Climate Change Adaptation and Resilience Enhancement","an increase in the capacity to adapt to climate change by enhancing resilience in the society",""],[1,"155","9","Natural Disaster Preparedness","preparations to respond to natural disasters",""]],"68":[[1,"145","4","Participation in Subregional Environmental Cooperation Agreements","Adhere to subregional agreements involving environmental cooperation frameworks such as the Core Environment Program and the Biodiversity Conservation Corridors Initiative under the GMS program and the Agreement on Cooperation for the Sustainable Development of the Mekong River Basin.",""],[1,"156","1","International Environmental Commitments Engagement","(8) enhancing the role of Thailand in international forums as they relate to commitments on the environment.",""]],"69":[[1,"57","3","Climate Change Adaptation Planning","Plans should be prepared to deal with problems caused by climate change.",""],[1,"57","3","Local Disaster Preparedness and Community Resilience","Local communities should be better prepared for natural disasters and climate change.",""],[1,"61","1","Climate Change and Natural Disaster Preparedness","The country should prepare to encounter climate change and natural disasters.",""],[1,"65","2","Climate Change and Disaster Preparedness Strengthening","Preparedness to cope with climate change and natural disasters is also essential for the society if it is to support economic development and a higher quality of life.",""],[1,"65","2","Adaptive Capacity Upgrade for Climate and Disaster Resilience","Adaptive capacity should be upgraded to handle climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"104","5","Climate Adaptation Support for Producers","Adaptations by producers should be enhanced to cope with climate change.",""]],"70":[[1,"89","8","Curriculum Improvement and Student-Centered Education Reform","Improve the curriculum and promote an educational system that is conducive to student development and is closely linked to societal needs and norms.",""],[1,"89","9","Talent Identification and Full Support for Children","Identify children with talent in sciences, mathematics, arts, crafts, sport, and music, and provide full support to enable them to reach their full potential.",""],[1,"90","1","Local Dialect and Language Promotion Programme","Promote the use and preservation of local dialects and proper Thai language usage, together with English as a second language, as well as other languages, especially those used in the ASEAN countries.",""],[1,"90","2","Teacher Quality Improvement and Training System","A program to produce high quality teachers should be supported.",""],[1,"90","2","Teacher Recruitment and Training System","A teacher training system should be undertaken to attract individuals who possess intellectual ability, morality, and a teaching spirit.",""],[1,"90","2","Teacher Excellence Recognition and Incentive Scheme","Sector partnerships should be promoted to honor excellence in teaching and dedicated teachers as role models.",""],[1,"90","2","Teacher Self-Improvement Incentives","Incentives should be offered to teachers for self-improvement, while the current assessment process should be improved to better achieve efficiency in education management and student development.",""],[1,"90","2","Education Assessment Process Improvement","Incentives should be offered to teachers for self-improvement, while the current assessment process should be improved to better achieve efficiency in education management and student development.",""],[1,"90","2","Private Sector Support for Quality Education","The private sector should be motivated to promote education that is focused on quality.",""],[1,"90","3","School Health and Hygiene Improvement","At school, sanitation should be improved to be more hygienic so the school environment will be better for student health.",""],[1,"95","6","Strengthen Regional and Provincial Educational Institutions","Encourage the roles of regional and provincial educational institutions to develop the individual, community, and society in a holistic manner.",""]],"71":[[1,"28","4","Human Resource Development for Lifelong Learning and Resilience","Develop human resources aimed at increasing resilience to deal with changes.",""],[1,"29","3","Lifelong Learning Promotion","5.2.4 Promote lifelong learning.",""],[1,"29","3","Early Childhood Learning Habit Development","Learning habits should be instilled in all Thais from an early age.",""],[1,"29","3","Alternative Education Expansion","The needs for alternative education should be addressed through the promotion of a society that wants to learn and through techniques conducive to lifelong learning.",""],[1,"29","4","Strengthening Social Institutions for Human Resource Development","Social institutions should be strengthened so as to develop human resources.",""],[1,"32","2","Workforce Improvement for Economic Restructuring","The country's competitive edge should be strengthened through development of financial and capital markets along with improvement in the workforce that will facilitate economic restructuring.",""],[1,"33","4","Educational Institution Capacity Enhancement","There is also a need to enhance the capacity of public and private educational institutions to meet internationally recognized standards.",""],[1,"33","4","Labor Skills Development and Product Standards Enforcement","In addition, labor skill development and minimum standards for goods and services are required in order to prevent the import of low-quality products into Thailand and neighboring countries.",""],[1,"75","3","Employment Information Access through Information Technology","Utilize a wide variety of information technology to support access to employment information.",""],[1,"90","4","Workforce Skills and Capacity Improvement","Improve skills and capacity in the workforce so it is better aligned with that needed for production of goods and services and is well-trained and creative to build a better economy.",""],[1,"90","5","Agricultural Workforce Capacity Building Programme","Build workforce capacity in the agricultural sector by increasing the number of new generation farmers, those who efficiently utilize modern knowledge and technology.",""],[1,"90","7","Semi-Skilled Labor Development through Skills Learning Incentives","Develop semi-skilled labor by promoting learning of skills, by creating incentives, enhancing the values of learning at the vocational",""],[1,"91","1","Vocational Qualification Standards Upgrade","Vocational qualification standards should be upgraded in order to develop competencies in workers that are relevant to targeted industries while expanding the needed specialties taught at vocational educational institutions.",""],[1,"91","1","Labor Force Development Networks","Networks that produce and develop the labor force should be created among various partners, particularly firms and special institutions, in parallel with international learning networks.",""],[1,"91","2","National Qualification Framework","Initiate a National Qualification Framework to ensure that education and competency qualifications are linked to demand to produce employees for specific career paths.",""],[1,"103","7","Agricultural Knowledge and Technology Enhancement","Develop and enhance knowledge, science and technology that is appropriate to agriculture.",""],[1,"103","7","Environmentally Sound Agricultural Technology Dissemination","Ensure the use of environmentally sound methods through technology distribution, learning centers and local networks of scholars.",""],[1,"103","7","Farmer Information Access Expansion","Farming knowledge should be developed and access to information for farmers should be widely expanded.",""],[1,"103","7","Agricultural Media Outreach for Technology and Innovation","Media interest in agriculture should be widespread to disseminate technology and innovation to farmers and the public.",""],[1,"124","3","Graduate Capability Enhancement Programme","Increase capabilities of graduates at all levels, especially in science and technology, in order to meet the needs of the agricultural, industrial and service sectors to assimilate changes in the labor market and technological advancement.",""],[1,"124","4","Public-Private Cooperation for Workforce Training and Specialized Expertise","Improve the quality of the labor force by encouraging cooperation between public and private academic institutions in training and building specialized expertise in order to increase the productivity of the workforce and enhance the competitiveness of the country.",""],[1,"124","4","Vocational Qualifications and Skilled Labor Standards Reform","In addition, the system of vocational qualifications and coherent skilled labor standards should be linked to remuneration and based on ability and performance.",""],[1,"124","5","National Labor Database Development","Create a national labor database covering both supply and demand and classified by economic sectors, educational attainments and vocational qualifications.",""],[1,"143","3","Public-Private Human Resource Development Partnership","Strengthen public-private participation to develop human resources in all economic sectors.",""],[1,"143","4","Capacity Enhancement for Educational Institutions","Enhance the capacity of public and private educational institutions to meet international standards.",""],[1,"144","4","International Labor Standards Cooperation and Regional Labor Mobility Plan","Accelerate cooperation in the establishment of international labor standards to facilitate regional labor mobility and increase the competitiveness of Thailand and neighboring countries.",""],[1,"144","4","Integrated Human Resources, Education, and Labor Skills Plan","An integrated plan with neighboring countries should be drafted on the development of human resources, education, and labor skills to enable economic restructuring of the country and the subregion and to prepare the workforce to cope with the transition toward an aging society in Thailand.",""]],"72":[[1,"178","3","Lifelong Learning for All Programme","1) to provide lifelong learning for all Thais;",""],[1,"184","3","Vocational Skills Training for Local Development","Vocational institutions should provide training in technological skills to assist local development.",""]],"73":[[1,"99","7","Strengthening Agricultural Sector Administrative Mechanisms","The agricultural sector's administrative mechanisms should have good governance.",""],[1,"102","2","Agricultural Land Use and Conservation Legislation Reform","Laws and regulations should be amended to encourage agricultural land utilization.",""],[1,"102","2","Accelerated Agricultural Land Protection Legislation","Legislation concerning the use, conservation and control of productive agricultural land should be accelerated while investment is made in infrastructure such as irrigation and transportation.",""],[1,"102","2","Agricultural Infrastructure Investment","investment is made in infrastructure such as irrigation and transportation.",""],[1,"103","3","Geography-Aligned Agricultural Production Support","Promote agricultural production that is in harmony with geography.",""]],"74":[[1,"14","2","Agricultural Sector Strengthening for Food and Energy Security","Strengthening of the agricultural sector to foster food and energy security with emphasis on management of natural resources, which are the basis for agriculture.",""],[1,"29","6","Arable Land Conservation and Equitable Land Redistribution","Productive arable lands should be conserved and small farmers should be supported and assured of the right to own farmland. Land should be redistributed equitably, and tax policies should be used to increase the efficiency of land utilization.",""],[1,"29","6","Agricultural Land Management Mechanism Improvement","Further, land management mechanisms should be improved.",""],[1,"29","6","Restoration of Agricultural Natural Resources and Good Farming Practices","Natural resources for agricultural production should be restored while good agricultural norms and practices should be promoted so as to support sustainable farming.",""],[1,"29","7","Agricultural Research and Development and Production Adaptation","Research and development should be emphasized while agricultural production should be modified according to socio-geographical conditions.",""],[1,"30","1","Agricultural Biodiversity and Climate-Smart Farming Promotion","Agricultural practices that preserve biodiversity and are suitable for the climate and the environment should be encouraged, while basic services for agricultural production should be improved.",""],[1,"30","1","Agricultural Science and Technology Development Support","Development of science and technology for agriculture is essential, including support for technologies for production whose utilizing is friendly to the environment.",""],[1,"56","1","Agricultural Revitalization and Food Security Strengthening","The agricultural sector should be invigorated and food security strengthened.",""],[1,"100","2","Agricultural Sector Efficiency and Food Security Programme","Empower the agricultural sector so that it becomes an efficient production base that can produce food and energy with value, quality, high standards and remain environmentally sound.",""],[1,"100","2","Market-Oriented Food Supply and Fair Trade Support","Production of the food supply should respond to market demands that incorporate fair trade and affordable prices.",""],[1,"100","3","Agricultural Household and Organization Strengthening for Sustainable Agriculture","Agricultural households and organizations will be strengthened and be self-reliant while practicing sustainable agriculture.",""],[1,"100","6","Sustainable Agricultural Area Expansion","Continually develop the quality and standards of commodities and food by expanding sustainable agricultural areas by at least 5 percent per year, and provide consumers access to safe and healthy food at fair prices.",""],[1,"100","7","Farmer Employment and Income Support","Secure employment and income for farmers so that they will be able to pay their debts and attract the younger generation to engage in agriculture.",""],[1,"105","6","Crop Insurance System Development","Accelerate the development of a crop insurance system.",""],[1,"105","7","Contract Farming Fairness Promotion","Promote fairness in the contract farming system.",""],[1,"105","8","Farmer Social Welfare and Debt Resolution Support","Develop a robust social welfare system and support the process for resolving their debts in order to develop self-reliance.",""],[1,"106","1","Young Farmer Attraction and Agricultural Skills Support","Attract young farmers and skilled labor to engage in farming.",""],[1,"106","1","Farmer Knowledge Sharing and Mindset Development Initiative","Create the appropriate mindset and enhance sharing knowledge.",""],[1,"106","1","Agricultural Land Access and Farm Financing Support","Arable land ready for cultivation should be provided while sources of funds should be readily accessible.",""],[1,"106","1","Farmer Image Promotion Campaign","A good public image for a career as a farmer should be projected.",""],[1,"106","1","Participatory Agricultural Planning Mechanism","Successful farmers should participate in setting agricultural development plans and actions.",""],[1,"106","2","Agricultural Institute and Cooperative Development Mechanism","Develop agricultural institutes, cooperatives, and small- and micro-community enterprises as mechanisms to enhance self-reliance and sustainability for farmers.",""]],"75":[[1,"25","6","Local Wisdom-Based Production and Services Development","To enhance the efficiency of production and services based on local wisdom, knowledge, innovation and creativity by developing food and energy security, while reforming the structure of economy so that consumption becomes more environmentally friendly, and strengthening relations with neighboring countries in the region for economic and social benefits.",""],[1,"30","2","Agricultural Value Chain Upgrading","Increase the value of agricultural commodities along supply chains.",""],[1,"30","2","Support for Local Agricultural Products, Food, and Energy","Local products and services in agricultural products, food and energy should be supported to create added value.",""],[1,"30","2","Agricultural Research and Development Collaboration","Local educational institutes and the private sector should collaborate on research and development while farmers and firms should apply knowledge, technologies and innovations that are environmentally sound.",""],[1,"30","2","Food Quality and Standards Upgrading","Food quality and standards for farm products relative to production systems should be upgraded to meet international standards.",""],[1,"30","2","Agricultural Market Strengthening","Present and future markets for agricultural commodities should be strengthened and the private sector, community organizations and agricultural institutes should participate in managing the food and commodity system.",""],[1,"30","2","Agricultural Logistics Efficiency Improvement","In addition, the efficiency of logistic management in the agricultural sector should be improved.",""],[1,"31","4","Agricultural Productivity and Green Value-Addition Initiative","In addition, it is necessary to improve productivity in the agricultural sector and to enhance value creation through innovation and green production processes.",""],[1,"102","7","Sustainable Agriculture and Fair Commodity Market Reform","Sustainable agricultural practices and fairness in commodity markets should be enhanced in order to increase competitiveness and self-reliance.",""],[1,"104","4","Agricultural Product Quality and Food Standards Upgrade","Increase the quality of agricultural products and food to meet international standards.",""],[1,"104","7","Standards Compliance Incentive Scheme for Farmers and Agribusinesses","Provide incentives for farmers and agro-businesses to produce goods and services that meet specific standards.",""],[1,"105","2","Central Trading Market and Agricultural Futures Market Strengthening","Strengthen the existing central trading markets and agricultural futures exchange market.",""],[1,"105","3","Community and Private Sector Agricultural Production and Food Management Partnership","Encourage communities and the private sector to play expanded roles in agricultural production and food management.",""],[1,"105","3","Fair Trade Cooperation with Agricultural Institutions","They should cooperate with agricultural institutions to enhance fair trade with farmers.",""],[1,"105","3","Eco-Friendly Agro-Industrial Production Promotion","Eco-friendly methods should be promoted that increase and extend agro-industrial production.",""],[1,"106","3","Food Processing Hub Promotion","Promote Thailand as a center for food processing within the forthcoming ASEAN Economic Community.",""],[1,"106","3","Imported Materials Handling Improvement","Procedures for handling imported materials should be improved.",""],[1,"106","3","Support for Small-Scale Farmers Affected by Trade Agreements","Small-scale farmers adversely affected by free trade agreements should be given assistance.",""],[1,"106","3","Farmer Adaptation Capacity Enhancement","The capability of farmers to adapt should be enhanced so they can produce basic commodities and food.",""],[1,"106","3","Food Standards Control System","In addition, a control system for food standards should be prominently featured to protect consumers from substandard imported goods.",""],[1,"120","5","Agricultural Productivity and Value-Added Improvement Programme","Improve the productivity of the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"121","3","Agro-Industry and New Business Development Initiative","Develop agro-industries and new businesses based on information, creativity, local insight and innovation to increase value-added, upgrade product quality, accommodate environmental concerns, meet international safety standards, and build market opportunities from the growth in demand for food that is forecast as world population increases.",""]],"76":[[1,"31","2","Bio-Energy Security and Crop Management System","Management systems for food and energy crops should be established.",""],[1,"31","2","Bio-Energy Crop Research and Development Programme","Research and development to increase the productivity of bio-energy crop production should be promoted.",""],[1,"31","2","Bio-Energy Price Regulation Mechanism","A mechanism to regulate the price structure of bio-energy should be created.",""],[1,"31","2","Public Awareness Campaign on Efficient Energy Use","Raise public awareness of the benefits of efficient energy use.",""],[1,"31","3","Public Management Reform for Food and Energy Security","Improve public management to enhance food and energy security.",""],[1,"31","3","Participatory Agricultural Development Planning","Farmers, local scholars, the private sector and local communities should participate in agricultural development planning.",""],[1,"31","3","Integrated Food and Energy Data Systems","Food and energy databases should be developed that span production and marketing through consumption.",""],[1,"31","3","Agricultural Law and Regulation Amendment Review","Amendments to laws and regulations that affect agricultural development should be considered.",""],[1,"31","3","International Cooperation for Food and Energy Security","International cooperation at bilateral and multilateral levels, particularly in the ASEAN community, should be encouraged in order to make food and energy secure.",""],[1,"107","2","Zero Waste Agriculture and Bioenergy Utilization","Promote the application of zero waste principles in agricultural activities.",""],[1,"107","3","Local Bio-energy Production from Refuse Support","Support local community efforts to produce bio-energy from refuse such as municipal solid waste and agricultural by-products through existing technology.",""],[1,"107","3","Community Power Plant Maintenance Capacity Building","Use of advanced knowledge for power plant maintenance should be provided for communities or local authorities in order to reduce the cost of generating power and alleviating pollution.",""],[1,"107","3","Non-food Energy Crop Planting Initiative","Non-food crops for fuel such as jatropha should be planted.",""],[1,"107","6","Energy Crop Productivity Research and Technology Application","Promote research and apply technology to increase energy crop productivity.",""],[1,"107","6","Alternative Renewable Energy Crop Research","Undertake research on other non-food crops as alternative sources of renewable energy such as algae in order to reduce food shortages.",""],[1,"107","7","Agricultural Product Management System for Food and Energy","Establish an agricultural product management system for food and energy.",""],[1,"107","8","Bioenergy Production Efficiency Enhancement","Enhance efficiency in bioenergy production.",""],[1,"107","9","Bioenergy Price Monitoring Mechanism","Provide mechanisms to monitor bioenergy prices.",""],[1,"108","1","Bioenergy Awareness and Knowledge Dissemination Initiative","Raise awareness of efficient bioenergy usage.",""],[1,"109","1","Food and Energy Security Support Measures","important to support research and development, cooperation in production, market access, emergency rice reserves, legislative reforms, and to strengthen existing mechanisms to enhance food and energy security.",""]],"77":[[1,"127","4","Business, Trade, and Investment Regulatory Reform","Amend laws, rules and regulations on business, trade and investment.",""],[1,"127","5","Regulatory and Incentive Reform for Production and Services","Adjust laws, rules, regulations and incentives in the production and service sectors.",""],[1,"127","5","Trade and Investment Risk Management through R&D","Ensure against risks in trade and investment, and in markets, through research and development based on knowledge and creativity.",""],[1,"127","5","Foreign Investment and Joint Venture Promotion","Investment from transnational corporations and foreign investors should be induced so they can establish joint ventures with the private sector, especially SMEs that have the potential to develop creative products and services.",""],[1,"127","5","Skilled Foreign Worker Immigration Facilitation","Skilled foreign workers should also be encouraged to immigrate to Thailand.",""],[1,"128","3","Transparent and Accountable Law Enforcement Reform","Strengthen law enforcement to be transparent and accountable through a publicly accepted process in order to respond to demands for social responsibility and conformity to international standards.",""],[1,"128","4","Law Enforcement Code of Conduct for Piracy Prevention","Apply a code of conduct for law enforcement that is equitable and unified and provides efficient protection and prevention of piracy in accordance with economic and social conditions, as well as international agreements.",""],[1,"128","5","Legal and Law Enforcement Capacity Development","Accelerate the development of legal experts and those involved in law enforcement in response to global changes.",""]],"78":[[1,"114","5","Fiscal Policy Implementation Efficiency and Tax Collection Improvement","Thailand must retain a strong fiscal position and use effective means of tax collection and budget allocation to support implementation of government policy and assist private economic activities.",""],[1,"129","6","National Revenue Collection Reform","Improvement of the system of national revenue collection by restructuring and reviewing the income and corporate tax rates.",""],[1,"130","1","Tax Base Expansion and Tax Reform","The tax base and excise taxes must also be adjusted in line with economic conditions, and allowances and tax exemptions should be revised.",""],[1,"130","1","Revenue Collection Efficiency Improvement","Greater efficiency in collecting revenue is essential.",""],[1,"130","1","New Social Equity Tax Schemes","Introduction of new tax schemes that can be used to create social equity should be accelerated; such schemes would include land and building taxes, property taxes and environmental taxes.",""],[1,"130","2","Priority-Based Budget Allocation and Management Reform","Enhance the effectiveness of budget allocation and management by prioritizing allocation in accordance with development issues that have high priority in the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"130","3","Fiscal Risk Prevention and Comprehensive Public Finance Assessment","Prevent fiscal risks by taking all risk factors of public finance into account.",""],[1,"130","4","State Enterprise Supervision and Risk Management System Reform","Improve the operational efficiency of state enterprises by developing systems of supervision and risk management that enhance transparency.",""],[1,"130","5","Private Sector Participation in Infrastructure and Public Services","Encourage the private sector to participate strongly in investment in infrastructure and basic public services such as education and public health by adjusting laws and regulations, and developing mechanisms and models.",""],[1,"130","6","Local Government Revenue Strengthening Reform","Strengthen the finances of local administrations by enhancing the efficiency and development of their sources of revenues in order to encourage them to rely on their own means rather than on subsidies from the government.",""],[1,"131","1","Environmental Tax Introduction","an environment tax must be levied",""],[1,"131","1","Local Fiscal Management Capacity Building","the capacity of local administration personnel concerning fiscal management must also be expanded",""],[1,"131","1","Results-Based Local Budget Reform","local budget procedure must be up-to-date and relevant to the government's budget system by using results-based budgeting and by encouraging public participation in the local administration budgeting process so it is transparent",""],[1,"131","1","Decentralized Local Debt Management Authority","proceeding to decentralizing authority for debt creation and debt management to local administration under certain restrictions",""]],"79":[[1,"34","6","Community and Local Government Empowerment for Development Planning","Strengthen domestic development partners at the community level.",""],[1,"34","6","Provincial and Cluster-Level Strategy Formulation Mechanism","The development mechanism for formulating strategies should be strengthened at the provincial and cluster levels, especially at border provinces, for cross border cooperation.",""]],"80":[[1,"28","2","Social Cohesion and Public Interaction Enhancement","Enhance social interaction among people within the society to bring about shared values and public benefits, and to reinforce effective, transparent, and accountable public administration.",""]],"81":[[1,"35","3","Low-Carbon Economic Transition","Shift the development paradigm and redirect the country to a low-carbon and environmentally friendly economy.",""]],"82":[[1,"25","7","Community-Based Natural Resource and Environmental Resilience Support","To build secure natural resource and environmental bases through supporting community participation and improving resilience that will cushion impacts from climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"35","2","Land Ownership and Marine and Coastal Resource Management Reform","Meanwhile, the management system governing land ownership and marine and coastal resources should undergo reform.",""]],"83":[[1,"6","2","Adaptive Sufficiency Economy Philosophy Development Strategy","In response, by continually adapting the Philosophy, Thailand will become more resilient and capable of managing risks through the application of knowledge, technology, innovation, creativity, and good governance.",""],[1,"12","1","Sufficiency Economy Philosophy Knowledge Dissemination and Curriculum Integration","There has been an effort to synthesize lessons learned from past practices and to establish a database system related to the Philosophy.","Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB)"],[1,"12","3","Implementation of the Philosophy of Sufficiency Economy","The Eleventh Plan will continue to implement the key elements of the \"Philosophy of Sufficiency Economy.\"",""],[1,"12","3","People-Centered Balanced Development Approach","It will place \"people at the center of development,\" and promote \"balanced development\" in all aspects.",""],[1,"12","3","Sufficiency Economy Principles Implementation","To achieve the outcomes that are envisioned, the Sufficiency Economy's principles will be further implemented.",""],[1,"12","3","Reasonableness in Analytical Work","First, \"reasonableness\" will be applied in analytical work;",""],[1,"12","3","Moderation for Balanced Development","\"moderation\" will be used to create a balance between material and spiritual dimensions, between societal self-dependence and global competitiveness, and between rural and urban societies;",""],[1,"12","3","Resilience Strengthening for Internal and External Change","\"resilience\" will be achieved by strengthening risk- taking ability in order to withstand internal and external changes.",""]],"84":[[1,"38","3","Stakeholder Capacity-Building for Development Participation","The potential of all stakeholders should be developed so they may take part effectively in the development process.",""],[1,"38","3","Community and Local Authority Empowerment Initiative","communities and local authority should be empowered to strengthen their responsiveness and adaptability toward any changes.",""],[1,"38","3","University-Community-Local Government Partnership","Academic institutions should play key roles in working with the community, local government, and provincial authorities and the role of the private sector should be enhanced for economic and social development.",""],[1,"38","3","Private Sector Engagement for Economic and Social Development","the role of the private sector should be enhanced for economic and social development.",""],[1,"38","3","Government Mindset Change for Development Leadership","government authorities need to adjust their mindset to play meaningful roles as agents of change for the country's development.",""],[1,"56","2","Community Empowerment and Social Development Capacity Building","The ability and potential of communities to develop various ways to enhance the quality of life and manage knowledge should be reinforced.",""],[1,"56","2","Civil Society Oversight of Public Agencies","Civil society should be energized to monitor the performance of public agencies and officials.",""],[1,"56","2","Community Integration into Regional and Global Development","Communities should be able to integrate their development within the context of economic developments in the Southeast Asian subregion, ASEAN, and worldwide.",""],[1,"63","6","Public Participation in Development Process","This strategy also places great emphasis on economic and social stability, equitable access to social services and social protection, adequate access to resources and infrastructure, unbiased and transparent access to the criminal justice system consistent with the public interest, and greater popular participation in the development process.",""],[1,"77","5","Citizen Participation and Civic Engagement Promotion","Key measures will seek to provide knowledge and understanding, promote the values of responsible citizenship, and reject wrongdoing and corruption.",""],[1,"77","5","Creative Ideas Sharing and Development Participation Events","Events should be arranged to share creative ideas and allow participation in various development organizations.",""],[1,"77","5","Inclusive Participation in Development Processes","People should be encouraged to participate in the country's development processes, ranging from initiating ideas, making decisions, setting guidelines, driving implementation, and overseeing government and development partner activities.",""],[1,"77","5","Inclusive Participation Opportunities for Vulnerable Groups","Moreover, children, youth, women, the disabled, older persons, the disadvantaged, the impoverished, and people in remote areas should be given opportunities to participate in all these activities.",""]],"85":[[1,"40","2","Social Development and Public Governance Strengthening","Some social problems need to be given continuous major effort.",""]],"86":[[1,"42","4","Human Resource Upgrading for Regional Integration","The first priority for Thailand is to develop its human resources, especially by upgrading education, linguistic and labor skills in order to cope with developments brought about by the emerging integration of Asian economies.",""],[1,"65","1","ASEAN Community Human Resource Development Preparation","it is crucial that Thailand prepare for the launching of the ASEAN Community, giving priority to human resource development in order to equip the population with the essential skills that will be in demand.",""],[1,"84","4","ASEAN Skilled Labor Mobility and Mutual Recognition Arrangements","In 2015, under agreed standards set for the ASEAN Economic Community, there will be a free flow of skilled labor in seven professions, with Mutual Recognition Arrangements (MRAs) for medical and dental practitioners and an MRA framework for accountants, engineers, nurses, architects, and surveyors.",""],[1,"84","4","Regional Skill Assessment Standard for Labor Migrants","there needs to be a skill assessment standard for labor migrants within the region.",""],[1,"91","2","ASEAN Labor Mobility Preparation","Preparation for the free flow of labor within the ASEAN Economic Community should be undertaken.",""],[1,"91","3","Labor Mobility Capacity Development","Thai workers should have the opportunity to develop their capacity for working abroad by learning professional and language skills.",""]],"87":[[1,"56","1","Economic Restructuring for Inclusive Quality Growth","The economy should be restructured to achieve quality and sustainability on an inclusive basis.",""],[1,"56","1","Service Sector Value-Added Enhancement","Value added in the service sector should be increased through creativity and innovation.",""],[1,"56","1","Grassroots Economy Expansion and Diversification","The grassroots economy should be enlarged; it should be resourceful and diversified.",""],[1,"56","1","Skills, Knowledge, and Infrastructure Access Promotion","Skill and knowledge in production and management as well as access to resources and infrastructure should be promoted.",""],[1,"56","1","Grassroots Finance and Savings System Reinforcement","Grassroots finance and saving systems should be reinforced to increase opportunity for secure and dignified work for citizens.",""],[1,"64","3","Economic Restructuring for Quality and Sustainability","This requires the use of science, technology, innovation, creativity and local knowledge as the driving forces conducive to maintaining the quality and sustainability of the environment and to a fair competitive system that can create resilience in the Thai economy.",""],[1,"64","3","Creative Services Value-Addition Initiative","Value should be added in the service sector based on creativity and innovation.",""],[1,"64","3","Creative Cities Development","Creative businesses and cities should be developed.",""],[1,"73","1","Access to Capital, Infrastructure, Skills and Knowledge for Secure Jobs","To provide access to sources of capital, infrastructure, skills and knowledge in order to build more secure jobs.",""],[1,"73","1","Business Opportunity Promotion Initiative","Business opportunities at all levels will also be promoted in order to enhance the quality of life for all people in the society.",""],[1,"73","5","Grassroots Economy Strengthening and Small Enterprise Support","the grass roots economy strengthened, and opportunities for communities and small enterprises enhanced.",""],[1,"74","8","Entrepreneurship, SME, and Community Enterprise Support","This can be achieved by creating opportunities for new entrepreneurs, assisting SMEs and community enterprises, and providing equal access to markets at all levels.",""],[1,"74","8","Grassroots Market Access Expansion","This can be achieved by creating opportunities for new entrepreneurs, assisting SMEs and community enterprises, and providing equal access to markets at all levels.",""],[1,"74","8","Manufacturing and Service Sector Job Creation Initiative","Emphasis should also be placed on job creation in the manufacturing and service sectors together with improvement in labor productivity and creativity in order to generate secure incomes for farmers.",""],[1,"78","2","Support for Community Enterprises and Occupational Groups","Promote the formation of occupational groups to utilize local resources in geographic areas based on their potential.",""],[1,"78","2","Integration of Local Knowledge and Culture in Community Enterprises","Local knowledge and culture should be integrated into community enterprises.",""],[1,"78","2","Value Chain Development Support for Occupational Groups","Development of occupational groups through production value chains should receive support.",""],[1,"95","3","Social Enterprise Promotion","Social enterprises should be encouraged to strike a balance between organizational and societal benefits.",""],[1,"104","2","Community Value-Addition Support for Food and Energy Production","Support communities who want to increase value in food and energy production.",""],[1,"104","2","Biodiversity-Based Local Product Development","Economic progress based on biodiversity and local knowledge should be promoted to create unique marketable assets such as herbal and food products, health and medical services and Halal foods and products.",""],[1,"104","2","Research and Development Support for Market Opportunities","Research and development should be supported to increase market opportunities and enhance competitiveness.",""],[1,"104","2","Niche Market High-Value Product Promotion","New higher value products that serve niche markets should be encouraged.",""]],"88":[[1,"56","1","Fair Wages, Welfare, and Labor Protection Reform","Wages and the welfare system should be fair, and labor protection should be adequate to ensure quality living.",""],[1,"75","4","Labor Rights Enforcement and Workplace Protection","In particular, ensure safety and sanitation conditions, regulation of working hours, and non- discrimination in wages and welfare, educational opportunities and training and re- training.",""],[1,"75","4","Worker Protection Regulatory and Enforcement Reform","To enhance productivity, regulations and enforcement should be improved to effectively protect workers under the principle of fundamental rights.",""],[1,"75","4","Inclusive Employment Opportunities for Older Persons, Women, and Persons with Disabilities","Job opportunities should be provided for older persons, women, and people with disabilities in order to utilize their potential.",""],[1,"75","5","Corporate Social Responsibility Incentives and Public Relations Campaign","A public relations campaign and tax incentives should be provided for those having corporate social responsibility activities in order to promote fair wages, safety and quality of life.",""]],"89":[[1,"57","2","Equitable Land Management Reform","The land management system should be improved through more equitable distribution.",""],[1,"57","2","Small Farmer Land Tenure Protection","Small farmers should be protected against loss of their land.",""],[1,"75","2","Property Rights Fairness and Land Registration Reform","Improve the fairness of property rights management.",""],[1,"102","2","Agricultural Land Conservation and Smallholder Land Access Reform","Conserve and protect productive agricultural land and support means for small-scale farmers to own land for cultivation or to have rights to arable land.",""],[1,"102","2","Land Management Law Enforcement Priority","Laws related to land management, particularly the Town Planning Act, should be an enforcement priority in order to preserve green areas and agricultural lands.",""],[1,"102","3","Agricultural Land Reform Expropriation and Land Tax Measures","Accelerate the process of expropriating private land for agricultural land reform.",""],[1,"102","4","Land Management Organization and Land Distribution System","Establish an organization and system for land management.",""]],"90":[[1,"57","4","Public Participation Anti-Corruption Mechanism","Mechanisms should be put in place through public participation to eradicate corruption.",""],[1,"57","4","Local Administration Decentralization and Empowerment","Decentralization should proceed and local administrations empowered to act on local concerns.",""],[1,"57","4","Equal Access to Justice Initiative","Citizens should have equal access to the judicial system and its resources.",""],[1,"61","2","National Good Governance and Public Sector Improvement","Fairness in administration at the national level should be promoted through good governance, with emphasis on improvement in the public sector and its managers.",""],[1,"61","2","Decentralization for Stronger Local Administration","Decentralization should be pursued more effectively in order to strengthen local administration.",""],[1,"61","2","Anti-Corruption Systems with Public Participation","Systems to deal with and prevent corruption should be developed through public participation.",""],[1,"61","2","Fair Access to Criminal Justice System","People should have fair access to the criminal justice system and its resources, while democratic values and good governance are promoted.",""],[1,"63","6","Just Society Promotion Strategy","This strategy aims to strengthen people at all levels - to give the individual, family, and community the capability to adjust to internal and external changes, cope with volatilities, and manage risks efficiently.",""],[1,"63","6","Transparent Access to Criminal Justice System","This strategy also places great emphasis on economic and social stability, equitable access to social services and social protection, adequate access to resources and infrastructure, unbiased and transparent access to the criminal justice system consistent with the public interest, and greater popular participation in the development process.",""],[1,"73","3","Public Administration Transparency Enhancement","Transparency in public administration and decision-making will be enhanced in accordance with the principles of legitimacy, ethics, morals and societal benefits.",""],[1,"73","7","Improved Access to Justice and Fair Law Enforcement","The population will realize its civic rights and duties, and have access to the judicial system rapidly and easily.",""],[1,"79","3","Public Administration Transparency and Accountability Reform","Enhance social interactions that recognize shared values and common interests, and reinforce effective, transparent, and accountable public administration.",""],[1,"80","2","Public Administration Efficiency and Transparency Reform","Strengthen the public administration system and enhance its efficiency with comprehensive checks and balances.",""],[1,"80","3","Public Budget Transparency and Spending Efficiency Improvement","Emphasis should be on increasing transparency and efficiency in spending the national budget, improving the performance appraisal system of government officials based on balance of power, and creating monitoring networks of independent organizations, civil society, academia, and the media.",""],[1,"80","3","Government Official Performance Appraisal Reform","Emphasis should be on increasing transparency and efficiency in spending the national budget, improving the performance appraisal system of government officials based on balance of power, and creating monitoring networks of independent organizations, civil society, academia, and the media.",""],[1,"80","3","Independent Monitoring Network for Public Accountability","Emphasis should be on increasing transparency and efficiency in spending the national budget, improving the performance appraisal system of government officials based on balance of power, and creating monitoring networks of independent organizations, civil society, academia, and the media.",""],[1,"80","4","Independent Monitoring Bodies Capacity Reform","Reform and enhance the capacity of independent monitoring bodies as partners in scrutinizing the government to end corruption.",""],[1,"80","6","Judicial Complaint and Remedy Access Mechanism","Ensure impartiality in the judicial system by making it easier for those adversely affected by the system to submit complaints and obtain remedies.",""],[1,"80","6","Legal Assistance for Affected Persons","To complement this effort, people should have the assistance of services such as prosecution, legal proceedings and execution of judgments.",""],[1,"81","2","Authority Monitoring Mechanism","A means to monitor the exercise of authority at every level needs to be developed.",""],[1,"81","2","Political Ethics and Integrity Promotion","Leadership, ethics, integrity, sacrifice, and the public interest should be embedded in the minds of politicians.",""],[1,"81","2","Sanctions for Self-Serving Political Conduct","Strong measures should be created to punish political parties and politicians who seek solely to fulfill their own interests by direct and indirect means.",""]],"91":[[1,"60","2","Agricultural Production and SME Strengthening","Economic progress will focus on strengthening agricultural production and SMEs.",""],[1,"60","2","Human Capital and Innovation Development","The abilities of the populace, their knowledge, and their advances in science and technological innovation and creativity will reinforce economic and social development.",""]],"92":[[1,"60","2","Regional and Global Economic Integration","At the same time, Thailand must connect with the regional and global economy, and observe its obligations under various international cooperation agreements.",""]],"93":[[1,"72","4","Equal Access to Public Services and Basic Infrastructure for Disadvantaged Groups","such groups will get fair and equal access to high quality public services, resources and the basic infrastructure",""],[1,"76","4","Public Service Quality and Access Improvement","Improve the quality of public services and broaden access to them.",""],[1,"76","4","Decentralization of Service Delivery Authority","Key measures should include promoting decentralization of authority.",""],[1,"76","4","National Health and Education Database Systems","It is also essential to develop national healthcare and educational database systems, distribute educational and healthcare resources, and introduce an incentive system to assign personnel and provide appropriate, sustainable pay and performance incentives.",""],[1,"89","2","Basic Regional Infrastructure and Social Services Development","Develop basic regional infrastructure and economic and social services to narrow the urban-rural development gap and reduce migration.",""]],"94":[[1,"75","6","Tax System Reform for Fairer Income Distribution","Reform the tax system to support a fair distribution of income and use it as a tool for enhancing resource allocation and property holdings.",""],[1,"75","6","Informal Worker and Micro-enterprise Tax Integration","Use databases to develop methods to bring informal workers and micro-enterprises into the tax system.",""],[1,"75","6","Needs-Based Budget Allocation Adjustment","The budget allocation process should be adjusted to reflect the special needs of geographic areas and target groups.",""]],"95":[[1,"76","1","Support Measures for Groups Harmed by Trade Liberalization","Develop methods to assist people and firms harmed by free trade agreements and investment liberalization.",""],[1,"76","1","Workforce Skills Upgrading for Employment","The workforce should be equipped with greater knowledge and skills needed for employment.",""],[1,"76","1","Private-Sector Cooperation for Occupational and Business Opportunities","Occupational and business opportunities should be created through cooperation with the private sector, with supporting funds available during a period of transition.",""]],"96":[[1,"56","2","Corporate Social Responsibility and Green Business Promotion","The private sector should be encouraged to undertake socially responsible and environmentally friendly businesses.",""],[1,"78","4","Responsible and Eco-Friendly Business Awareness Campaigns","Campaigns should be designed to create awareness of responsible and eco-friendly business activities.",""],[1,"78","4","Anti-Corruption Engagement by Private Sector and Civil Society","Meanwhile, the private sector and civil society should be encouraged to identify and suppress corruption at all levels.",""],[1,"79","1","Corporate Social Responsibility Promotion","corporate social responsibility should be promoted.",""],[1,"95","3","Multi-Stakeholder Cooperation for Social Responsibility","Promote cooperation among civil society, businesses, and government agencies.",""],[1,"95","3","Private Sector Engagement in Worker Learning and Living Arrangements","The involvement of the private sector in learning management and living arrangements for workers is essential.",""],[1,"95","3","Media Incentives for Socially Responsible Enterprises and Philanthropists","Praise and rewards via media should be incentives for socially responsible private enterprises and philanthropists.",""]],"97":[[1,"78","5","Consumer Rights Protection Enforcement Enhancement","Increase the standards of consumer rights protection to accommodate the free flow of goods, services, and information in the ASEAN community.",""],[1,"79","1","Consumer Rights Information and Complaint Surveillance Improvement","Access to information about consumer rights and protection should be increased while surveillance of complaints should be improved.",""],[1,"79","1","Consumer Rights Awareness and Public Participation Support","Awareness of and popular participation in consumer's rights protection should be supported,",""],[1,"79","1","Health and Environmental Impact Assessment and Regulation of Goods and Services","the health and environmental impacts from using goods and services should be assessed and regulated as needed.",""],[1,"79","1","Regulatory Update for Changing Goods and Services","Rules and regulations should be amended to correspond to changes in the nature of goods and services",""]],"98":[[1,"79","5","Democratic Culture and Constitutional Rights Promotion","Progress can be made by strengthening the democratic conscience and culture of the populace and politicians.",""],[1,"81","2","Political Rights and Duties Awareness Programme","To achieve this ambition, it is necessary to create knowledge and awareness concerning political rights and duties at the community, local and national levels.",""],[1,"81","2","Popular Participation in Policy and Budget Decisions","Popular participation should be encouraged in public policy discussions and budget decisions.",""]],"99":[[1,"81","3","Social Media Support for Development and Responsible Information Sharing","Support the use of social media at local and national levels to reinforce development.",""],[1,"95","8","Social Network Engagement and Online Learning Support","Strengthen the role of social networks in reflecting public demands and expressing creative opinions.",""]],"100":[[1,"88","7","Fertility Choice and Population Distribution Policy","Improve the demographic structure and population distribution.",""],[1,"88","8","Fertility Rate Maintenance and Childbearing Encouragement","Encourage more childbearing by couples capable of creating or expanding a family and maintain fertility rates at least at the current rate.",""],[1,"88","9","Reproductive Health and Family Support Measures","Promote quality reproductive health for all ages and establish appropriate tax and child care assistance measures that encourage couples to have children and give them a quality childhood.",""],[1,"88","10","Family Studies and Reproductive Health Education Promotion","Promote knowledge in family studies, nutritional education, behavioral reproductive health, sexual health, and the preparation of parents at the pre-pregnancy, pregnancy, delivery, and post-delivery stages.",""]],"101":[[1,"89","1","Regional Employment Promotion and Reverse Migration Incentives","Increase regional employment opportunities to reduce outward migration and provide incentives for reverse migration.",""]],"102":[[1,"75","4","ASEAN Cooperation on Skills Development for Inclusive Economic Participation","Regional cooperation with ASEAN to encourage participation of these groups in economic activities should be promoted in areas of skill development.",""],[1,"91","4","Foreign Worker Management Improvement Programme","Improve management of foreign workers in a systematic manner that includes registering unskilled workers, providing incentives to attract professional and high skilled workers, improvement of the data base system, and provision of social services in an appropriate and equitable manner.",""]],"103":[[1,"92","6","Public Health Service Improvement Programme","Improve public health services to provide better quality and coverage.",""],[1,"92","6","Primary Care Services Development","Emphasis should be placed on the development of primary care services, alternative medicines, geriatric medicines, and health information systems.",""],[1,"92","6","Health Workforce Expansion and Redistribution","Health personnel should be increased and distributed to best utilize their services.",""],[1,"92","6","Health Worker Incentive Package","Incentives such as good compensation and fringe benefits should be provided.",""],[1,"92","6","Efficient Health Financing Measures","Financial measures involving health care should be utilized efficiently.",""]],"104":[[1,"94","6","Community and Local Public Recreation Space Support","Support community and local administrative organizations to provide public spaces for recreational activities for the family and community.",""],[1,"94","6","Business-Sector Public Benefit Activity Promotion","The business sector should organize activities of benefit to the public that include family participation.",""],[1,"94","7","Community Identity and Local Wisdom Preservation Initiative","Seek and shape community identity and strengthen its learning processes.",""]],"105":[[1,"87","6","Moral Values and Public Virtues Promotion","To ensure that family, religious institutions, and academic institutions play important roles by instilling moral values and public virtues in children and all Thais.",""],[1,"88","6","Sufficiency Economy Human Capacity Development","Emphasis should be on the adoption of the Philosophy of Sufficiency Economy to reinforce human capacity in all its diverse dimensions, including physical health, knowledge, morality, perseverance, and resilience.",""],[1,"88","6","Strengthening Social Institutions for Human Resource Development","Social institutions should also be strengthened to introduce an environment conducive to the development of human resources.",""],[1,"95","4","Religious Institutions and Moral Education Support","Revive the roles of religious institutions in instilling morality and serving as spiritual sanctuaries.",""],[1,"95","4","Religious Practice Space and Guidance Provision","Set out accurate religious principles and provide space for religious practices.",""],[1,"95","4","Child Morality and Integrity Learning Activities","Innovations and learning activities should be developed to promote morality and integrity in children.",""],[1,"95","7","Family, School, and Religious Institution Cooperation for Civic and Moral Development","Promote mutual cooperation among family, educational institutions, and religious institutions to develop thinking based on morality, acceptance of diverse cultures, consciousness of citizenship, and democratic culture.",""],[1,"95","9","International Cultural Networks for Mutual Understanding","International cultural networks, especially among members of the ASEAN community, should be created to enable the free flow of cultural information and ideas for mutual understanding involving history, culture, and sharing of knowledge.",""]],"106":[[1,"103","4","Pesticide Registration System Improvement","The pesticide registration system should be improved to ensure that registered hazardous substances in other countries are not allowed to be used in Thailand.",""],[1,"103","4","Control of Agricultural Chemical Advertising and Market Promotion","Advertising and market promotion should be controlled so they are in accord with principles of the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO).",""],[1,"103","4","Promotion of Organic Material Use in Farming","The use of organic material should be increased to reduce production costs.",""],[1,"103","4","Agricultural Food Safety Assurance","Food safety for both producers and consumers should be assured.",""],[1,"103","4","Farmer Training on Proper Pesticide Use","farmers should have thorough knowledge about the proper use of pesticides.",""],[1,"105","1","Food Safety Information Dissemination and Certification Fee Reduction","should be disseminated and certification fees should be reduced in order to increase the quality and control the safety of food production.",""]],"107":[[1,"104","6","Livestock Production Value-Addition and Safety Improvement","Create more value in livestock production.",""]],"108":[[1,"108","3","Participatory Agricultural Planning and Monitoring Mechanism","Encourage farmers, networks of local scholars, the private sector, and local communities to participate in establishing guidelines and plans for agricultural production that will enhance food and energy security at the community and national levels.",""],[1,"108","4","Interagency Coordination for Food and Energy Security","They should proactively cooperate and integrate development guidelines for food and energy security.",""],[1,"108","4","Multi-Stakeholder Implementation Mechanism","Implementation mechanisms should be established among government agencies, the private sector and farmers.",""],[1,"108","4","Community Monitoring of Government Implementation","The government's implementation should be monitored through community participation.",""],[1,"108","5","Food and Energy Information Database and Early Warning System","Develop a database of food and energy information and a system to ensure accuracy.",""],[1,"108","6","Agricultural Development Legislation and Regulatory Reform","Enact laws related to agricultural development that will foster sustainable development.",""],[1,"108","7","International Cooperation with ASEAN Economic Community","Encourage international cooperation at the multilateral and bilateral levels.",""]],"109":[[1,"113","4","Financial Rules and Regulations Reform for Basel III Compliance","Thus, Thailand will need to reform financial rules and regulations to meet the international accords of Basel III.",""],[1,"114","6","Financial System Development and Capital Market Master Plans","Thailand has to maintain stable and efficient financial and capital markets, and must accelerate the implementation of the Financial System Master Plan Phase II and Capital Market Master Plan so that these markets can act as major sources of capital and provide financial services equitably to all sectors.",""],[1,"114","6","Strengthening the Financial Foundation for Sustainable Growth","At the same time, a strong financial foundation must be established to facilitate sustainable growth and to manage risks and limitations that may arise both internally and externally.",""],[1,"123","4","Financial and Capital Market Development for Sector Restructuring","Develop financial and capital markets that facilitate the restructuring of the production and service sectors, and serve as alternative mechanisms for saving.",""],[1,"123","5","Financial Sector Infrastructure and Safeguards Development","Develop stable and efficient financial institutions by building infrastructure and safeguards that facilitate service delivery and human resource development in the financial sector.",""],[1,"123","5","Electronic Financial Services Promotion","Financial services through electronic channels should be promoted.",""],[1,"123","5","Financial Market Master Plan Phase II Acceleration","Implementation of the Financial Market Master Plan Phase II and the Specialized Financial Institution Master Plan should be accelerated.",""],[1,"123","5","Financial Institution Risk Management Reform","The risk management system of financial institutions should be reformed and strictly enforced.",""],[1,"128","2","Capital Market Legal and Regulatory Reform","Reform monetary and fiscal laws regarding the growth of capital markets.",""],[1,"128","7","Timely Monetary Policy Management","Implement appropriate monetary policies to respond to economic circumstances in a timely manner to maintain price stability and a sound financial system, and stimulate economic growth.",""],[1,"128","8","Capital Market Expansion and Modernization","Increase the role of capital markets in the economy in keeping with the direction of global financial development and upgrade their role so it will be relevant to other countries in the region.",""],[1,"129","1","Financial Sector Legal and Regulatory Reform","Improve the nation's financial foundation by reforming laws and regulations, the tax system, the management system, and accounting standards so they are responsive to the competitive environment.",""],[1,"129","1","Capital Market Development and Regulatory Transparency Reform","develop capital markets, and reform the regulatory system so it is clear, transparent, and serves as a hedge against any risk factors to monetary policy and the macro-economy and is relevant to international standards.",""],[1,"129","2","Economic Surveillance and Early Warning System","Develop surveillance mechanisms to spot economic fluctuations and develop a holistic warning system that covers all risks, such as the exposure of financial institutions, the fiscal system, and the functioning of the manufacturing and service sectors, that are crucial to the country.",""],[1,"129","2","Linked Economic Database Systems","In order to develop such a warning system, it is vital to develop linked database systems that can provide in-depth analysis.",""],[1,"129","3","Capital Flow Management Regulatory Reform","Increase the effectiveness of capital flow management by revising regulations that limit the use of capital inflows and overseas investments, and utilize international reserves.",""],[1,"129","3","Sovereign Wealth Fund Feasibility Study","A feasibility study on establishing a sovereign wealth fund should be undertaken",""],[1,"129","3","Infrastructure Fund Support for State Enterprises","capable state enterprises should be supported when establishing infrastructure funds.",""],[1,"129","3","Short-Term Capital Inflow Controls and Exchange Rate Risk Instruments","strict controls on short-term inflows and the development of financial instruments to manage exchange rate risks are still necessary when revising regulations to encourage the private sector to utilize available foreign resources.",""],[1,"129","4","Asian Bond Market Expansion and Regional Currency Settlement","Asian currencies should be enhanced in international markets by expanding the volume and liquidity of the Asian bond market and by using Asian hard currencies for exchange settlements in order to select one currency in the region for settling most cross border economic transactions.",""],[1,"129","5","National Savings and Investment Management Framework","Manage national savings and investment so it is responsive to economic growth and offers protection against any future crises.",""],[1,"135","4","Financial and Investment Capacity and Security Development","Efforts are also underway to develop capacity and security in finance and investment in order to facilitate modern, high quality economic development of the country in the long run.",""]],"110":[[1,"117","3","Trade and Investment Sector Restructuring","Restructure the trade and investment sectors in accordance with the opportunities from the expansion of Asian, African, and the Thai domestic economies.",""],[1,"117","4","Market Efficiency and Distribution Expansion to New Export Markets","Improve the efficiency of the market and the distribution of production to Asian and African markets.",""],[1,"117","5","Export Market Development and Product Differentiation Initiative","Develop goods and services to meet the demands of new markets.",""],[1,"117","6","Free Trade Agreement Activation and Enterprise Support","Accelerate activation of free trade agreements (FTAs) and be prepared for their impact.",""],[1,"118","5","Business Research and Development Support","Build the competitive advantage of businesses to be more creative by supporting research and development.",""],[1,"118","5","Knowledge and New Technology Adoption Initiative","Promote the application of knowledge and new technologies, and invest in high potential businesses.",""],[1,"118","5","International Market Competitiveness Expansion","Moreover, competitive advantages should be fully exploited in international markets such as tourism, healthcare services, logistic services, the film industry, and the meeting, incentive, convention, and exhibition (MICE) industry.",""],[1,"118","6","Export Market Expansion and Competitiveness Support for Thai Firms","Expand production and marketing of high-potential businesses to overseas buyers by developing the competitive advantages of Thai firms throughout the supply chain.",""],[1,"118","6","Financial and Tax Support for Export Competitiveness","Provide financial support and tax measures that competitors in other countries enjoy.",""],[1,"118","6","Overseas Business Network Expansion","New markets should be explored and networks of business partnerships should be strengthened in order to expand overseas business in services.",""],[1,"135","4","Thailand-ASEAN Asia-Pacific Market Promotion Policy","Thailand and ASEAN member countries have jointly implemented a common policy that aims to promote interest in potential markets in the Asia-Pacific region.",""],[1,"135","5","Support for Doha Round Multilateral Trade Negotiations","Free trade and investment are given importance through support of the Doha-round multilateral trade negotiations.",""],[1,"139","2","Thai Firm Competitiveness Support","The government shall provide support for Thai enterprises and those of neighboring countries in areas under joint development.",""],[1,"139","5","ASEAN Trade and Investment Promotion","To enhance the interests of Thailand in international trade, investment, finance, and market opportunities through ASEAN membership, and through trade and investment that connects with the new economic superpowers in Asia and groups of emerging economies in the Asia-Pacific region.",""],[1,"140","5","Business Cost Reduction to Meet International Standards","The cost of doing business will be reduced at national and subregional levels to meet international standards.",""],[1,"144","5","Support for Thai Firms Investing Abroad","Provide support for Thai firms that undertake investment abroad, especially in neighboring countries, in order to solve problems of labor and raw material shortages.",""],[1,"145","6","Free Trade Agreement Utilization and SME Adjustment Support","Accelerate the use of currently effective free trade agreements.",""],[1,"146","1","Support for Foreign Investors' Regional Operations Offices","Assist foreign investors to establish regional operations offices so as to enhance the country's capacity to become an investment hub for the region and bring in foreign currencies.",""]],"111":[[1,"119","4","Cluster Development for Local Production and Service Linkages","Strengthen local communities, small enterprises and public personnel so they can link the production and service sectors at the area level via the cluster development approach.",""],[1,"119","4","Human Resource Skills Development for Public and Local Actors","Develop the skills and knowledge of human resources in the public sector, local governments, and communities, and also in small and medium enterprises so they can cope with impacts that arise from changing world economic conditions.",""],[1,"119","5","Innovative Business Cluster Development","Support the development of innovative businesses through cluster development by strengthening links and cooperation among businesses along the supply chain.",""],[1,"119","5","Creative Industry Knowledge and Resource Sharing Initiative","In addition, sharing of knowledge, the uses of creativity, and merging of resources among related industries should be reinforced in production, distribution and commercialization.",""],[1,"119","5","Fair Competition and Standards Upgrade Policy","The promotion of fair competition should also be emphasized as an important tool to upgrade quality and standards of production.",""],[1,"119","5","Institutional Redefinition for Creative Clusters","The roles of appropriate institutions and agencies should be redefined to support creative clusters.",""],[1,"119","6","Creative Cities Development Initiative","Promote development of creative cities by establishing ecological principles that are applied to physical infrastructure, human resources, regulations and management.",""],[1,"120","1","Knowledge-Oriented Urban Infrastructure Development","Also, infrastructures that emphasize knowledge and support the learning process should be set up.",""],[1,"120","1","Creative Learning Centers and Innovation Exhibition Spaces","These will provide a creative environment with learning centers, imaginative spaces, and exhibitions and trade fairs that feature innovation in products and services.",""],[1,"120","2","Business and Creative Economy Innovation Support Programme","Support businesses and personnel that apply new methods to increase the value of their products and services by upgrading the skills and knowledge within firms, especially SMEs.",""],[1,"120","2","Creative Personnel Support Along Innovative Industry Supply Chains","Give similar support to key creative personnel along the supply chain of innovative industries, that is, those involved in design, research and development, fresh methods, business administration, technology and marketing.",""],[1,"120","2","Creative Economy Research and Business Database Development","Support research regarding development of the creative economy and compile a comprehensive database on businesses with fresh ideas.",""],[1,"120","3","Creative Industries Financing Support System","Put in place a financial system that will support investment in the development of creative industries by helping these businesses gain access to financial sources.",""]],"112":[[1,"121","3","Industrial Cluster Enterprise Network Development","This could be accomplished by encouraging industrial clusters to form enterprise networks and cooperate among businesses and related agencies.",""],[1,"121","3","Research and Development Promotion in Production and Processing","This would facilitate promoting research and development in production and processing.",""],[1,"121","4","Manufacturing Industrial Infrastructure Development","Develop industrial infrastructure in the manufacturing sector to promote production efficiency and higher standards.",""],[1,"121","4","Manufacturing Innovation and Value Addition Initiative","Science, technology and innovation should be applied to create value in manufactured products and decrease the import of goods.",""],[1,"121","4","Public-Private-Academic Workforce Skills Cooperation","Effective cooperation among the public and private sectors and academic institutions should be enhanced to improve skills, creativity and knowledge in the workforce.",""],[1,"121","5","Enterprise Linkage and Regional Industrial Decentralization Programme","Support links between large enterprises and local ones, and induce industries to locate regional facilities.",""],[1,"121","5","SME and OTOP Supply Chain Integration Initiative","Link small and medium enterprises (SMEs) and One Tambon One Product (OTOP) firms with large industrial companies throughout the supply chain;",""],[1,"139","1","Regional Competitive Production Base Development","Utilize potential economic advantages from geographical location and the ability of areas in various regions of Thailand to create a competitive domestic base of production.",""],[1,"139","1","Food Processing, Tourism, Health Services, and IT Promotion","In particular, promote food processing, tourism, health services, and information technology.",""],[1,"139","1","Regional Planning and Inter-Framework Coordination","This development will require planning that will ensure that the opportunity and capacity of each region is consistent, as well as coordination among various cooperative frameworks.",""],[1,"139","1","Border Town Development for Economic Corridors","It is also necessary to develop border towns that are linked to cities and communities in the regions of Thailand that are part of the economic corridors.",""],[1,"143","2","Cross-Border Production Cluster Development","Development of production clusters with the cooperation of neighboring countries should be considered when these countries are capable of doing so.",""],[1,"143","2","Cross-Border Supply Chain Product Development","product development in cross-border supply chains should take into consideration subregional and other export markets.",""]],"113":[[1,"143","3","ASEAN Knowledge Dissemination Initiative","Knowledge of all aspects of ASEAN should be disseminated.",""],[1,"143","3","Trade and Investment Competitiveness Awareness Measures","The business sector should make better use of the openness in trade, investment, and services, awareness of intellectual property, and trends toward market expansion and future agreements.",""],[1,"143","3","Agricultural Price and Supply Stabilization Measures","Measures should be put in place to deal with fluctuations in price for agricultural products and to cope with shortages in energy and agricultural products due to the free flow of goods.",""],[1,"143","5","Import Quality Standards and Joint Labor Qualification System","Set minimum standards for goods and services in order to prevent the import of low quality products into Thailand and its neighbors that may cause loss of life, damage to property, and pollution.",""]],"114":[[1,"144","6","Protection and Support for Thai Nationals and Communities Abroad","Protect the rights and interests of Thai people and labor abroad, and strengthen Thai communities in foreign countries by providing information about local laws, supporting activities for Thai people, and enhancing the ability of Thai communities to live abroad with dignity and a good quality of life.",""],[1,"144","6","Skills, Insurance, and Assistance for Thai Workers Abroad","Efforts should also be made to improve vocational and linguistic skills, provide insurance and protect Thais working abroad, monitor and assist those in trouble, and guard their rights.",""]],"115":[[1,"153","2","Climate Change Information Database Systems","Database systems that incorporate information, technology, and local wisdom in response to impacts from climate change.",""],[1,"153","2","Physical Infrastructure and Ecosystem Rehabilitation Investments","Moreover, investments should be made in physical infrastructure and in rehabilitation of the ecosystem - forest restoration, coastal protection, a remedy for saline soil, water supply development, flood and drought alleviation and restoration of the balance of nature.",""],[1,"153","4","Climate Change and Natural Resource Governance Instruments","Instruments and management mechanisms to deal with climate change and governance of natural resources and the environment.",""],[1,"156","1","Trade Resilience for Environmental and Climate Change Adaptation","(7) creation of resilience in trade in order to respond to conditions created by environmental and climate change;",""]],"116":[[1,"157","2","Community-Based Coastal Zone Management","Communities should participate in the management of local coastal zones for sustainable fisheries.",""],[1,"157","2","Coastal Construction Standards Improvement","Standards of construction in both communities and industrial areas, as well as coastal infrastructure, should be improved by addressing the effects of oceanographic changes and coastal erosion.",""],[1,"157","2","Long-Term Coastal Sea-Level Rise Response Planning","Planning long-term responses to rising sea levels is necessary to reduce damage to coastal urban areas.",""]],"117":[[1,"159","4","Expand Government Procurement for Environmentally Beneficial Products","Government procurement programs for local government should be expanded to motivate such production and crops.",""],[1,"159","4","Tax Incentives for Environmentally Friendly Products","Firms should be afforded tax benefits when their products are environmentally friendly to create better competition.",""],[1,"159","4","Awards Criteria for Environmentally Progressive Agencies","Criteria for giving awards to environmentally progressive government agencies should be established.",""],[1,"159","4","Private Sector Environmentally Beneficial Procurement Support","Private enterprises should be asked to support environmentally beneficial procurement throughout the supply chain.",""],[1,"161","2","Sustainable Consumption Attitude Change Campaign","Undertake a campaign to change attitudes to create an understanding of the value of sustainable consumption as the norm in the society.",""],[1,"161","3","Environmental Information and Sustainable Consumption Awareness Campaign","Publicize information and transfer knowledge to people about the environment and sustainable consumption so as to enhance their ability to choose environmentally desirable products and services.",""],[1,"161","4","Consumer Protection Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthen consumer protection mechanisms and support networks, media, advertising and public relations to redirect society toward sustainable consumption.",""]],"118":[[1,"162","2","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Planning","Support formulation of long-term plans to cope with climate change and emphasize its economic and social impacts.",""],[1,"163","2","Adaptive Capacity Support for Vulnerable Groups","Upgrade the adaptive capacity of vulnerable groups by allocating adequate resources and communicate information concerning risks and risk management from various agencies to communities and their learning networks.",""],[1,"163","2","Recovery Assistance and Livelihood Restoration","For areas that have been harmed, recovery assistance should be provided, including restoration of natural resources and ensuring employment for those at risk of losing their livelihoods.",""],[1,"163","3","Community Risk Management Measures","Provide short- and long-term measures to deal with damages to the community and society.",""],[1,"163","4","Long-Term Community Planning Support","Support long-term community planning.",""]],"119":[[1,"164","4","Environmental Preservation Monitoring and Trade Coordination Measures","Monitor indices of environmental preservation, so as not to impinge on international trade and investment.",""],[1,"164","5","Border Carbon Adjustment and Carbon Labeling Measures","Create measures to cope with the anticipated effects on trade measures and international agreements from environmental protection and climate change, particularly a border carbon tax, as defined by the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT).",""],[1,"164","6","Trade Agreement Impact Mitigation Planning","Conduct research into the effects of international agreements on trade, and develop strategic plans to alleviate impacts on affected products and businesses.",""],[1,"164","6","Promotion of Environmentally Sound Goods and Services","At the same time, environmentally sound goods and services and their industries should be promoted.",""],[1,"164","6","Strategic Investment Alliances for Green Technology","Thailand should have strategic investment alliances with countries that are advanced in environmentally friendly technology.",""],[1,"164","7","Export Carbon Footprint Disclosure Support","Encourage exporters to include carbon footprint information.",""],[1,"164","7","Small-Scale Exporter Certification Support","Financial support, information and facilities should be provided to certify small-scale exporters.",""],[1,"164","7","Source-Level Carbon Accounting Promotion","Carbon accounting should be promoted at the source of raw materials, especially as it concerns agriculture and fisheries.",""],[1,"164","7","Product Verification and Certification System","A system of product verification and certification should be developed.",""],[1,"164","8","Incentives for Innovative Sustainable Industries","Generate incentives to create innovative industries that practice sustainable development.",""],[1,"164","8","Research and Development Support for Carbon Credit Trading Businesses","Research and development should be supported to expand trade and investment in businesses that deal in carbon credit trading.",""],[1,"178","3","ASEAN Economic Community Preparedness Initiative","6) to prepare Thailand to become a part of the ASEAN Economic Community;",""]],"120":[[1,"165","2","International Negotiation Analysis and Monitoring Mechanism","Analyze details of agreements, and monitor the status of negotiations with other nations.",""],[1,"165","3","Government Officials Negotiation Skills Strengthening","Strengthen government officials' negotiating skills.",""],[1,"165","4","ASEAN and Major Trading Partner Cooperation Development","Develop cooperation within ASEAN and with major trading partners.",""]],"121":[[1,"166","3","Hazardous, Electronic, and Infected Waste Management System","Establish a management system for hazardous, electronic and infected wastes.",""],[1,"166","4","Integrated Chemicals Management System","Integrated management of chemicals should be inaugurated and the import of high-risk agricultural chemicals restricted or terminated.",""],[1,"166","4","Agency Chemical Database Linkage","Chemical databases should be developed by each agency and linked to cover sources - upstream to downstream - involving import, production, operation, and disposal.",""],[1,"166","4","Chemical Risk Information Dissemination and Surveillance System","Information about the risks of hazardous chemicals in production processes should be disseminated to industries while consumers should be protected by establishment of a social network and system of surveillance to monitor the safety of chemicals and products.",""],[1,"166","5","Pollution Accident Warning and Management System","Create a warning system together with a management system to address pollution accidents at both national and local levels.",""],[1,"166","5","Pollution Emergency Response Capacity Building","Personnel should have the means and ability to respond to emergencies.",""],[1,"166","5","Pollution Accident Remediation and Victim Compensation Measures","Measures should be ready to remedy, rehabilitate and restore the environment and compensate and make whole the victims of pollution accidents.",""],[1,"166","5","Polluter-Pays Environmental Fund","A fund should be established comprised of revenue from industries and factories that have been polluters.",""],[1,"168","1","Environmental Tax Collection and Pollution Fee Reform","Accelerate collection of environmental taxes and reform the national budget to create incentives for efficient use of natural resources and reduction of pollution.",""]],"122":[[1,"167","2","Community Natural Resource Management Support","Empower communities and support local rights to utilize natural resources in a balanced and sustainable manner.",""],[1,"167","2","Biodiversity-Based Local Economic Development Promotion","Utilization of natural resources and biodiversity-based economic developments should be fostered and take into account local lifestyle, knowledge, and traditional culture.",""],[1,"167","2","Community Ecosystem Information and Resource Database Development","Information about the ecosystem should be provided to communities.",""],[1,"167","2","Local Natural Resource and Biodiversity Survey and Database Initiative","LAOs and their communities should survey their natural resources, biodiversity and local knowledge to develop databases.",""],[1,"167","3","Community Participation and Capacity Development","Support popular participation and develop community abilities.",""],[1,"167","3","Multi-Stakeholder Land Management Mechanism","Land management mechanisms should be established and comprised of the government and private sectors, academia, the local administration and its populace.",""],[1,"167","3","Local Community Environmental Councils","Local community environmental councils should be established to hold public hearings concerning government development projects.",""],[1,"167","3","Public Awareness Campaign on Natural Resource Protection","Mass media should be used to raise public awareness about protecting natural resources and the environment.",""],[1,"167","3","Local Authority Natural Resource Management Powers","The LAOs should have authority to manage natural resources and the environment.",""],[1,"184","1","Community Empowerment and Local Self-Management Programme","Communities should be strengthened through information and the ability to manage their affairs, and benefit from knowledge from outside sources through local research networks.",""],[1,"184","1","Local Knowledge Sharing and Research Network Promotion","Sharing of knowledge should be promoted at all levels to support accomplishments and manage risks.",""],[1,"184","1","Community-Led Local Implementation and Cooperation Mechanism","Local citizens should undertake their own implementation.",""],[1,"184","1","Citizen-Local Authority-Academic Cooperation Framework","Cooperation among citizens, LAOs, and local academic institutions should be encouraged.",""]]}});